module ExaltedBook40

public func ExaltedBook40Chapter(c: Int32) -> String {
  switch c {
    case 1: return s"1{|}The book of the generation of Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham.{|}2{|}Abraham begat Isaac; and Isaac begat Jacob; and Jacob begat Judas and his brethren;{|}3{|}And Judas begat Phares and Zara of Thamar; and Phares begat Esrom; and Esrom begat Aram;{|}4{|}And Aram begat Aminadab; and Aminadab begat Naasson; and Naasson begat Salmon;{|}5{|}And Salmon begat Booz of Rachab; and Booz begat Obed of Ruth; and Obed begat Jesse;{|}6{|}And Jesse begat David the king; and David the king begat Solomon of her that had been{~}the wife of Urias;{|}7{|}And Solomon begat Roboam; and Roboam begat Abia; and Abia begat Asa;{|}8{|}And Asa begat Josaphat; and Josaphat begat Joram; and Joram begat Ozias;{|}9{|}And Ozias begat Joatham; and Joatham begat Achaz; and Achaz begat Ezekias;{|}10{|}And Ezekias begat Manasses; and Manasses begat Amon; and Amon begat Josias;{|}11{|}And Josias begat Jechonias and his brethren, about the time they were carried away to{~}Babylon:{|}12{|}And after they were brought to Babylon, Jechonias begat Salathiel; and Salathiel begat{~}Zorobabel;{|}13{|}And Zorobabel begat Abiud; and Abiud begat Eliakim; and Eliakim begat Azor;{|}14{|}And Azor begat Sadoc; and Sadoc begat Achim; and Achim begat Eliud;{|}15{|}And Eliud begat Eleazar; and Eleazar begat Matthan; and Matthan begat Jacob;{|}16{|}And Jacob begat Joseph the husband of Mary, of whom was born Jesus, who is called{~}Christ.{|}17{|}So all the generations from Abraham to David are fourteen generations; and from David{~}until the carrying away into Babylon are fourteen generations; and from the carrying{~}away into Babylon unto Christ are fourteen generations.{|}18{|}Now the birth of Jesus Christ was on this wise: When as his mother Mary was espoused to{~}Joseph, before they came together, she was found with child of the Holy Ghost.{|}19{|}Then Joseph her husband, being a just man, and not willing to make her a publick{~}example, was minded to put her away privily.{|}20{|}But while he thought on these things, behold, the angel of the Lord appeared unto him in{~}a dream, saying, Joseph, thou son of David, fear not to take unto thee Mary thy wife:{~}for that which is conceived in her is of the Holy Ghost.{|}21{|}And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name JESUS: for he shall save{~}his people from their sins.{|}22{|}Now all this was done, that it might be fulfilled which was spoken of the Lord by the{~}prophet, saying,{|}23{|}Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son, and they shall call{~}his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, God with us.{|}24{|}Then Joseph being raised from sleep did as the angel of the Lord had bidden him, and{~}took unto him his wife:{|}25{|}And knew her not till she had brought forth her firstborn son: and he called his name{~}JESUS.";
    case 2: return s"1{|}Now when Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judaea in the days of Herod the king, behold,{~}there came wise men from the east to Jerusalem,{|}2{|}Saying, Where is he that is born King of the Jews? for we have seen his star in the{~}east, and are come to worship him.{|}3{|}When Herod the king had heard these things, he was troubled, and all Jerusalem with him.{|}4{|}And when he had gathered all the chief priests and scribes of the people together, he{~}demanded of them where Christ should be born.{|}5{|}And they said unto him, In Bethlehem of Judaea: for thus it is written by the prophet,{|}6{|}And thou Bethlehem, in the land of Juda, art not the least among the princes of Juda:{~}for out of thee shall come a Governor, that shall rule my people Israel.{|}7{|}Then Herod, when he had privily called the wise men, enquired of them diligently what{~}time the star appeared.{|}8{|}And he sent them to Bethlehem, and said, Go and search diligently for the young child;{~}and when ye have found him, bring me word again, that I may come and worship him also.{|}9{|}When they had heard the king, they departed; and, lo, the star, which they saw in the{~}east, went before them, till it came and stood over where the young child was.{|}10{|}When they saw the star, they rejoiced with exceeding great joy.{|}11{|}And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother,{~}and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they{~}presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.{|}12{|}And being warned of God in a dream that they should not return to Herod, they departed{~}into their own country another way.{|}13{|}And when they were departed, behold, the angel of the Lord appeareth to Joseph in a{~}dream, saying, Arise, and take the young child and his mother, and flee into Egypt, and{~}be thou there until I bring thee word: for Herod will seek the young child to destroy{~}him.{|}14{|}When he arose, he took the young child and his mother by night, and departed into Egypt:{|}15{|}And was there until the death of Herod: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken of{~}the Lord by the prophet, saying, Out of Egypt have I called my son.{|}16{|}Then Herod, when he saw that he was mocked of the wise men, was exceeding wroth, and{~}sent forth, and slew all the children that were in Bethlehem, and in all the coasts{~}thereof, from two years old and under, according to the time which he had diligently{~}enquired of the wise men.{|}17{|}Then was fulfilled that which was spoken by Jeremy the prophet, saying,{|}18{|}In Rama was there a voice heard, lamentation, and weeping, and great mourning, Rachel{~}weeping for her children, and would not be comforted, because they are not.{|}19{|}But when Herod was dead, behold, an angel of the Lord appeareth in a dream to Joseph in{~}Egypt,{|}20{|}Saying, Arise, and take the young child and his mother, and go into the land of Israel:{~}for they are dead which sought the young child’s life.{|}21{|}And he arose, and took the young child and his mother, and came into the land of Israel.{|}22{|}But when he heard that Archelaus did reign in Judaea in the room of his father Herod, he{~}was afraid to go thither: notwithstanding, being warned of God in a dream, he turned{~}aside into the parts of Galilee:{|}23{|}And he came and dwelt in a city called Nazareth: that it might be fulfilled which was{~}spoken by the prophets, He shall be called a Nazarene.";
    case 3: return s"1{|}In those days came John the Baptist, preaching in the wilderness of Judaea,{|}2{|}And saying, Repent ye: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.{|}3{|}For this is he that was spoken of by the prophet Esaias, saying, The voice of one crying{~}in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make his paths straight.{|}4{|}And the same John had his raiment of camel’s hair, and a leathern girdle about his{~}loins; and his meat was locusts and wild honey.{|}5{|}Then went out to him Jerusalem, and all Judaea, and all the region round about Jordan,{|}6{|}And were baptized of him in Jordan, confessing their sins.{|}7{|}But when he saw many of the Pharisees and Sadducees come to his baptism, he said unto{~}them, O generation of vipers, who hath warned you to flee from the wrath to come?{|}8{|}Bring forth therefore fruits meet for repentance:{|}9{|}And think not to say within yourselves, We have Abraham to our father: for I say unto{~}you, that God is able of these stones to raise up children unto Abraham.{|}10{|}And now also the axe is laid unto the root of the trees: therefore every tree which{~}bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire.{|}11{|}I indeed baptize you with water unto repentance: but he that cometh after me is mightier{~}than I, whose shoes I am not worthy to bear: he shall baptize you with the Holy Ghost,{~}and with fire:{|}12{|}Whose fan is in his hand, and he will throughly purge his floor, and gather his wheat{~}into the garner; but he will burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire.{|}13{|}Then cometh Jesus from Galilee to Jordan unto John, to be baptized of him.{|}14{|}But John forbad him, saying, I have need to be baptized of thee, and comest thou to me?{|}15{|}And Jesus answering said unto him,{~}{r}Suffer it to be so now: for thus it becometh us to fulfil all righteousness.{/r}{~}Then he suffered him.{|}16{|}And Jesus, when he was baptized, went up straightway out of the water: and, lo, the{~}heavens were opened unto him, and he saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove, and{~}lighting upon him:{|}17{|}And lo a voice from heaven, saying, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.";
    case 4: return s"1{|}Then was Jesus led up of the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted of the devil.{|}2{|}And when he had fasted forty days and forty nights, he was afterward an hungred.{|}3{|}And when the tempter came to him, he said, If thou be the Son of God, command that these{~}stones be made bread.{|}4{|}But he answered and said,{~}{r}It is written, Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceedeth out{/r}{~}{r}of the mouth of God.{/r}{|}5{|}Then the devil taketh him up into the holy city, and setteth him on a pinnacle of the{~}temple,{|}6{|}And saith unto him, If thou be the Son of God, cast thyself down: for it is written, He{~}shall give his angels charge concerning thee: and in their hands they shall bear thee{~}up, lest at any time thou dash thy foot against a stone.{|}7{|}Jesus said unto him,{~}{r}It is written again, Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God.{/r}{|}8{|}Again, the devil taketh him up into an exceeding high mountain, and sheweth him all the{~}kingdoms of the world, and the glory of them;{|}9{|}And saith unto him, All these things will I give thee, if thou wilt fall down and{~}worship me.{|}10{|}Then saith Jesus unto him,{~}{r}Get thee hence, Satan: for it is written, Thou shalt worship the Lord thy God, and him{/r}{~}{r}only shalt thou serve.{/r}{|}11{|}Then the devil leaveth him, and, behold, angels came and ministered unto him.{|}12{|}Now when Jesus had heard that John was cast into prison, he departed into Galilee;{|}13{|}And leaving Nazareth, he came and dwelt in Capernaum, which is upon the sea coast, in{~}the borders of Zabulon and Nephthalim:{|}14{|}That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Esaias the prophet, saying,{|}15{|}The land of Zabulon, and the land of Nephthalim, by the way of the sea, beyond Jordan,{~}Galilee of the Gentiles;{|}16{|}The people which sat in darkness saw great light; and to them which sat in the region{~}and shadow of death light is sprung up.{|}17{|}From that time Jesus began to preach, and to say,{~}{r}Repent: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.{/r}{|}18{|}And Jesus, walking by the sea of Galilee, saw two brethren, Simon called Peter, and{~}Andrew his brother, casting a net into the sea: for they were fishers.{|}19{|}And he saith unto them,{~}{r}Follow me, and I will make you fishers of men.{/r}{|}20{|}And they straightway left their nets, and followed him.{|}21{|}And going on from thence, he saw other two brethren, James the son of Zebedee, and John{~}his brother, in a ship with Zebedee their father, mending their nets; and he called{~}them.{|}22{|}And they immediately left the ship and their father, and followed him.{|}23{|}And Jesus went about all Galilee, teaching in their synagogues, and preaching the gospel{~}of the kingdom, and healing all manner of sickness and all manner of disease among the{~}people.{|}24{|}And his fame went throughout all Syria: and they brought unto him all sick people that{~}were taken with divers diseases and torments, and those which were possessed with{~}devils, and those which were lunatick, and those that had the palsy; and he healed them.{|}25{|}And there followed him great multitudes of people from Galilee, and from Decapolis, and{~}from Jerusalem, and from Judaea, and from beyond Jordan.";
    case 5: return s"1{|}And seeing the multitudes, he went up into a mountain: and when he was set, his{~}disciples came unto him:{|}2{|}And he opened his mouth, and taught them, saying,{|}3{|}{r}Blessed are the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.{/r}{|}4{|}{r}Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted.{/r}{|}5{|}{r}Blessed are the meek: for they shall inherit the earth.{/r}{|}6{|}{r}Blessed are they which do hunger and thirst after righteousness: for they shall be{/r}{~}{r}filled.{/r}{|}7{|}{r}Blessed are the merciful: for they shall obtain mercy.{/r}{|}8{|}{r}Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see God.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}Blessed are the peacemakers: for they shall be called the children of God.{/r}{|}10{|}{r}Blessed are they which are persecuted for righteousness’ sake: for theirs is the kingdom{/r}{~}{r}of heaven.{/r}{|}11{|}{r}Blessed are ye, when men shall revile you, and persecute you, and shall say all manner{/r}{~}{r}of evil against you falsely, for my sake.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}Rejoice, and be exceeding glad: for great is your reward in heaven: for so persecuted{/r}{~}{r}they the prophets which were before you.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}Ye are the salt of the earth: but if the salt have lost his savour, wherewith shall it{/r}{~}{r}be salted? it is thenceforth good for nothing, but to be cast out, and to be trodden{/r}{~}{r}under foot of men.{/r}{|}14{|}{r}Ye are the light of the world. A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid.{/r}{|}15{|}{r}Neither do men light a candle, and put it under a bushel, but on a candlestick; and it{/r}{~}{r}giveth light unto all that are in the house.{/r}{|}16{|}{r}Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your{/r}{~}{r}Father which is in heaven.{/r}{|}17{|}{r}Think not that I am come to destroy the law, or the prophets: I am not come to destroy,{/r}{~}{r}but to fulfil.{/r}{|}18{|}{r}For verily I say unto you, Till heaven and earth pass, one jot or one tittle shall in no{/r}{~}{r}wise pass from the law, till all be fulfilled.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}Whosoever therefore shall break one of these least commandments, and shall teach men so,{/r}{~}{r}he shall be called the least in the kingdom of heaven: but whosoever shall do and teach{/r}{~}{r}them, the same shall be called great in the kingdom of heaven.{/r}{|}20{|}{r}For I say unto you, That except your righteousness shall exceed the righteousness of the{/r}{~}{r}scribes and Pharisees, ye shall in no case enter into the kingdom of heaven.{/r}{|}21{|}{r}Ye have heard that it was said by them of old time, Thou shalt not kill; and whosoever{/r}{~}{r}shall kill shall be in danger of the judgment:{/r}{|}22{|}{r}But I say unto you, That whosoever is angry with his brother without a cause shall be in{/r}{~}{r}danger of the judgment: and whosoever shall say to his brother, Raca, shall be in danger{/r}{~}{r}of the council: but whosoever shall say, Thou fool, shall be in danger of hell fire.{/r}{|}23{|}{r}Therefore if thou bring thy gift to the altar, and there rememberest that thy brother{/r}{~}{r}hath ought against thee;{/r}{|}24{|}{r}Leave there thy gift before the altar, and go thy way; first be reconciled to thy{/r}{~}{r}brother, and then come and offer thy gift.{/r}{|}25{|}{r}Agree with thine adversary quickly, whiles thou art in the way with him; lest at any{/r}{~}{r}time the adversary deliver thee to the judge, and the judge deliver thee to the officer,{/r}{~}{r}and thou be cast into prison.{/r}{|}26{|}{r}Verily I say unto thee, Thou shalt by no means come out thence, till thou hast paid the{/r}{~}{r}uttermost farthing.{/r}{|}27{|}{r}Ye have heard that it was said by them of old time, Thou shalt not commit adultery:{/r}{|}28{|}{r}But I say unto you, That whosoever looketh on a woman to lust after her hath committed{/r}{~}{r}adultery with her already in his heart.{/r}{|}29{|}{r}And if thy right eye offend thee, pluck it out, and cast it from thee: for it is{/r}{~}{r}profitable for thee that one of thy members should perish, and not that thy whole body{/r}{~}{r}should be cast into hell.{/r}{|}30{|}{r}And if thy right hand offend thee, cut it off, and cast it from thee: for it is{/r}{~}{r}profitable for thee that one of thy members should perish, and not that thy whole body{/r}{~}{r}should be cast into hell.{/r}{|}31{|}{r}It hath been said, Whosoever shall put away his wife, let him give her a writing of{/r}{~}{r}divorcement:{/r}{|}32{|}{r}But I say unto you, That whosoever shall put away his wife, saving for the cause of{/r}{~}{r}fornication, causeth her to commit adultery: and whosoever shall marry her that is{/r}{~}{r}divorced committeth adultery.{/r}{|}33{|}{r}Again, ye have heard that it hath been said by them of old time, Thou shalt not forswear{/r}{~}{r}thyself, but shalt perform unto the Lord thine oaths:{/r}{|}34{|}{r}But I say unto you, Swear not at all; neither by heaven; for it is God’s throne:{/r}{|}35{|}{r}Nor by the earth; for it is his footstool: neither by Jerusalem; for it is the city of{/r}{~}{r}the great King.{/r}{|}36{|}{r}Neither shalt thou swear by thy head, because thou canst not make one hair white or{/r}{~}{r}black.{/r}{|}37{|}{r}But let your communication be, Yea, yea; Nay, nay: for whatsoever is more than these{/r}{~}{r}cometh of evil.{/r}{|}38{|}{r}Ye have heard that it hath been said, An eye for an eye, and a tooth for a tooth:{/r}{|}39{|}{r}But I say unto you, That ye resist not evil: but whosoever shall smite thee on thy right{/r}{~}{r}cheek, turn to him the other also.{/r}{|}40{|}{r}And if any man will sue thee at the law, and take away thy coat, let him have thy cloke{/r}{~}{r}also.{/r}{|}41{|}{r}And whosoever shall compel thee to go a mile, go with him twain.{/r}{|}42{|}{r}Give to him that asketh thee, and from him that would borrow of thee turn not thou away.{/r}{|}43{|}{r}Ye have heard that it hath been said, Thou shalt love thy neighbour, and hate thine{/r}{~}{r}enemy.{/r}{|}44{|}{r}But I say unto you, Love your enemies, bless them that curse you, do good to them that{/r}{~}{r}hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and persecute you;{/r}{|}45{|}{r}That ye may be the children of your Father which is in heaven: for he maketh his sun to{/r}{~}{r}rise on the evil and on the good, and sendeth rain on the just and on the unjust.{/r}{|}46{|}{r}For if ye love them which love you, what reward have ye? do not even the publicans the{/r}{~}{r}same?{/r}{|}47{|}{r}And if ye salute your brethren only, what do ye more than others? do not even the{/r}{~}{r}publicans so?{/r}{|}48{|}{r}Be ye therefore perfect, even as your Father which is in heaven is perfect.{/r}";
    case 6: return s"1{|}{r}Take heed that ye do not your alms before men, to be seen of them: otherwise ye have no{/r}{~}{r}reward of your Father which is in heaven.{/r}{|}2{|}{r}Therefore when thou doest thine alms, do not sound a trumpet before thee, as the{/r}{~}{r}hypocrites do in the synagogues and in the streets, that they may have glory of men.{/r}{~}{r}Verily I say unto you, They have their reward.{/r}{|}3{|}{r}But when thou doest alms, let not thy left hand know what thy right hand doeth:{/r}{|}4{|}{r}That thine alms may be in secret: and thy Father which seeth in secret himself shall{/r}{~}{r}reward thee openly.{/r}{|}5{|}{r}And when thou prayest, thou shalt not be as the hypocrites are: for they love to pray{/r}{~}{r}standing in the synagogues and in the corners of the streets, that they may be seen of{/r}{~}{r}men. Verily I say unto you, They have their reward.{/r}{|}6{|}{r}But thou, when thou prayest, enter into thy closet, and when thou hast shut thy door,{/r}{~}{r}pray to thy Father which is in secret; and thy Father which seeth in secret shall reward{/r}{~}{r}thee openly.{/r}{|}7{|}{r}But when ye pray, use not vain repetitions, as the heathen do: for they think that they{/r}{~}{r}shall be heard for their much speaking.{/r}{|}8{|}{r}Be not ye therefore like unto them: for your Father knoweth what things ye have need of,{/r}{~}{r}before ye ask him.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}After this manner therefore pray ye: Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy{/r}{~}{r}name.{/r}{|}10{|}{r}Thy kingdom come. Thy will be done in earth, as it is in heaven.{/r}{|}11{|}{r}Give us this day our daily bread.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}And forgive us our debts, as we forgive our debtors.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil: For thine is the kingdom, and{/r}{~}{r}the power, and the glory, for ever. Amen.{/r}{|}14{|}{r}For if ye forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you:{/r}{|}15{|}{r}But if ye forgive not men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your{/r}{~}{r}trespasses.{/r}{|}16{|}{r}Moreover when ye fast, be not, as the hypocrites, of a sad countenance: for they{/r}{~}{r}disfigure their faces, that they may appear unto men to fast. Verily I say unto you,{/r}{~}{r}They have their reward.{/r}{|}17{|}{r}But thou, when thou fastest, anoint thine head, and wash thy face;{/r}{|}18{|}{r}That thou appear not unto men to fast, but unto thy Father which is in secret: and thy{/r}{~}{r}Father, which seeth in secret, shall reward thee openly.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon earth, where moth and rust doth corrupt, and{/r}{~}{r}where thieves break through and steal:{/r}{|}20{|}{r}But lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust doth corrupt,{/r}{~}{r}and where thieves do not break through nor steal:{/r}{|}21{|}{r}For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.{/r}{|}22{|}{r}The light of the body is the eye: if therefore thine eye be single, thy whole body shall{/r}{~}{r}be full of light.{/r}{|}23{|}{r}But if thine eye be evil, thy whole body shall be full of darkness. If therefore the{/r}{~}{r}light that is in thee be darkness, how great is that darkness!{/r}{|}24{|}{r}No man can serve two masters: for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or{/r}{~}{r}else he will hold to the one, and despise the other. Ye cannot serve God and mammon.{/r}{|}25{|}{r}Therefore I say unto you, Take no thought for your life, what ye shall eat, or what ye{/r}{~}{r}shall drink; nor yet for your body, what ye shall put on. Is not the life more than{/r}{~}{r}meat, and the body than raiment?{/r}{|}26{|}{r}Behold the fowls of the air: for they sow not, neither do they reap, nor gather into{/r}{~}{r}barns; yet your heavenly Father feedeth them. Are ye not much better than they?{/r}{|}27{|}{r}Which of you by taking thought can add one cubit unto his stature?{/r}{|}28{|}{r}And why take ye thought for raiment? Consider the lilies of the field, how they grow;{/r}{~}{r}they toil not, neither do they spin:{/r}{|}29{|}{r}And yet I say unto you, That even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of{/r}{~}{r}these.{/r}{|}30{|}{r}Wherefore, if God so clothe the grass of the field, which to day is, and to morrow is{/r}{~}{r}cast into the oven, shall he not much more clothe you, O ye of little faith?{/r}{|}31{|}{r}Therefore take no thought, saying, What shall we eat? or, What shall we drink? or,{/r}{~}{r}Wherewithal shall we be clothed?{/r}{|}32{|}{r}(For after all these things do the Gentiles seek:) for your heavenly Father knoweth that{/r}{~}{r}ye have need of all these things.{/r}{|}33{|}{r}But seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall{/r}{~}{r}be added unto you.{/r}{|}34{|}{r}Take therefore no thought for the morrow: for the morrow shall take thought for the{/r}{~}{r}things of itself. Sufficient unto the day is the evil thereof.{/r}";
    case 7: return s"1{|}{r}Judge not, that ye be not judged.{/r}{|}2{|}{r}For with what judgment ye judge, ye shall be judged: and with what measure ye mete, it{/r}{~}{r}shall be measured to you again.{/r}{|}3{|}{r}And why beholdest thou the mote that is in thy brother’s eye, but considerest not the{/r}{~}{r}beam that is in thine own eye?{/r}{|}4{|}{r}Or how wilt thou say to thy brother, Let me pull out the mote out of thine eye; and,{/r}{~}{r}behold, a beam is in thine own eye?{/r}{|}5{|}{r}Thou hypocrite, first cast out the beam out of thine own eye; and then shalt thou see{/r}{~}{r}clearly to cast out the mote out of thy brother’s eye.{/r}{|}6{|}{r}Give not that which is holy unto the dogs, neither cast ye your pearls before swine,{/r}{~}{r}lest they trample them under their feet, and turn again and rend you.{/r}{|}7{|}{r}Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened{/r}{~}{r}unto you:{/r}{|}8{|}{r}For every one that asketh receiveth; and he that seeketh findeth; and to him that{/r}{~}{r}knocketh it shall be opened.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}Or what man is there of you, whom if his son ask bread, will he give him a stone?{/r}{|}10{|}{r}Or if he ask a fish, will he give him a serpent?{/r}{|}11{|}{r}If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children, how much more{/r}{~}{r}shall your Father which is in heaven give good things to them that ask him?{/r}{|}12{|}{r}Therefore all things whatsoever ye would that men should do to you, do ye even so to{/r}{~}{r}them: for this is the law and the prophets.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth{/r}{~}{r}to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat:{/r}{|}14{|}{r}Because strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few{/r}{~}{r}there be that find it.{/r}{|}15{|}{r}Beware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep’s clothing, but inwardly they are{/r}{~}{r}ravening wolves.{/r}{|}16{|}{r}Ye shall know them by their fruits. Do men gather grapes of thorns, or figs of thistles?{/r}{|}17{|}{r}Even so every good tree bringeth forth good fruit; but a corrupt tree bringeth forth{/r}{~}{r}evil fruit.{/r}{|}18{|}{r}A good tree cannot bring forth evil fruit, neither can a corrupt tree bring forth good{/r}{~}{r}fruit.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}Every tree that bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire.{/r}{|}20{|}{r}Wherefore by their fruits ye shall know them.{/r}{|}21{|}{r}Not every one that saith unto me, Lord, Lord, shall enter into the kingdom of heaven;{/r}{~}{r}but he that doeth the will of my Father which is in heaven.{/r}{|}22{|}{r}Many will say to me in that day, Lord, Lord, have we not prophesied in thy name? and in{/r}{~}{r}thy name have cast out devils? and in thy name done many wonderful works?{/r}{|}23{|}{r}And then will I profess unto them, I never knew you: depart from me, ye that work{/r}{~}{r}iniquity.{/r}{|}24{|}{r}Therefore whosoever heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them, I will liken him unto{/r}{~}{r}a wise man, which built his house upon a rock:{/r}{|}25{|}{r}And the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that{/r}{~}{r}house; and it fell not: for it was founded upon a rock.{/r}{|}26{|}{r}And every one that heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them not, shall be likened{/r}{~}{r}unto a foolish man, which built his house upon the sand:{/r}{|}27{|}{r}And the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that{/r}{~}{r}house; and it fell: and great was the fall of it.{/r}{|}28{|}And it came to pass, when Jesus had ended these sayings, the people were astonished at{~}his doctrine:{|}29{|}For he taught them as one having authority, and not as the scribes.";
    case 8: return s"1{|}When he was come down from the mountain, great multitudes followed him.{|}2{|}And, behold, there came a leper and worshipped him, saying, Lord, if thou wilt, thou{~}canst make me clean.{|}3{|}And Jesus put forth his hand, and touched him, saying,{~}{r}I will; be thou clean.{/r}{~}And immediately his leprosy was cleansed.{|}4{|}And Jesus saith unto him,{~}{r}See thou tell no man; but go thy way, shew thyself to the priest, and offer the gift{/r}{~}{r}that Moses commanded, for a testimony unto them.{/r}{|}5{|}And when Jesus was entered into Capernaum, there came unto him a centurion, beseeching{~}him,{|}6{|}And saying, Lord, my servant lieth at home sick of the palsy, grievously tormented.{|}7{|}And Jesus saith unto him,{~}{r}I will come and heal him.{/r}{|}8{|}The centurion answered and said, Lord, I am not worthy that thou shouldest come under my{~}roof: but speak the word only, and my servant shall be healed.{|}9{|}For I am a man under authority, having soldiers under me: and I say to this man, Go, and{~}he goeth; and to another, Come, and he cometh; and to my servant, Do this, and he doeth{~}it.{|}10{|}When Jesus heard it, he marvelled, and said to them that followed,{~}{r}Verily I say unto you, I have not found so great faith, no, not in Israel.{/r}{|}11{|}{r}And I say unto you, That many shall come from the east and west, and shall sit down with{/r}{~}{r}Abraham, and Isaac, and Jacob, in the kingdom of heaven.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}But the children of the kingdom shall be cast out into outer darkness: there shall be{/r}{~}{r}weeping and gnashing of teeth.{/r}{|}13{|}And Jesus said unto the centurion,{~}{r}Go thy way; and as thou hast believed, so be it done unto thee.{/r}{~}And his servant was healed in the selfsame hour.{|}14{|}And when Jesus was come into Peter’s house, he saw his wife’s mother laid, and sick of a{~}fever.{|}15{|}And he touched her hand, and the fever left her: and she arose, and ministered unto{~}them.{|}16{|}When the even was come, they brought unto him many that were possessed with devils: and{~}he cast out the spirits with his word, and healed all that were sick:{|}17{|}That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Esaias the prophet, saying, Himself took{~}our infirmities, and bare our sicknesses.{|}18{|}Now when Jesus saw great multitudes about him, he gave commandment to depart unto the{~}other side.{|}19{|}And a certain scribe came, and said unto him, Master, I will follow thee whithersoever{~}thou goest.{|}20{|}And Jesus saith unto him,{~}{r}The foxes have holes, and the birds of the air have nests; but the Son of man hath not{/r}{~}{r}where to lay his head.{/r}{|}21{|}And another of his disciples said unto him, Lord, suffer me first to go and bury my{~}father.{|}22{|}But Jesus said unto him,{~}{r}Follow me; and let the dead bury their dead.{/r}{|}23{|}And when he was entered into a ship, his disciples followed him.{|}24{|}And, behold, there arose a great tempest in the sea, insomuch that the ship was covered{~}with the waves: but he was asleep.{|}25{|}And his disciples came to him, and awoke him, saying, Lord, save us: we perish.{|}26{|}And he saith unto them,{~}{r}Why are ye fearful, O ye of little faith?{/r}{~}Then he arose, and rebuked the winds and the sea; and there was a great calm.{|}27{|}But the men marvelled, saying, What manner of man is this, that even the winds and the{~}sea obey him!{|}28{|}And when he was come to the other side into the country of the Gergesenes, there met him{~}two possessed with devils, coming out of the tombs, exceeding fierce, so that no man{~}might pass by that way.{|}29{|}And, behold, they cried out, saying, What have we to do with thee, Jesus, thou Son of{~}God? art thou come hither to torment us before the time?{|}30{|}And there was a good way off from them an herd of many swine feeding.{|}31{|}So the devils besought him, saying, If thou cast us out, suffer us to go away into the{~}herd of swine.{|}32{|}And he said unto them,{~}{r}Go.{/r}{~}And when they were come out, they went into the herd of swine: and, behold, the whole{~}herd of swine ran violently down a steep place into the sea, and perished in the waters.{|}33{|}And they that kept them fled, and went their ways into the city, and told every thing,{~}and what was befallen to the possessed of the devils.{|}34{|}And, behold, the whole city came out to meet Jesus: and when they saw him, they besought{~}him that he would depart out of their coasts.";
    case 9: return s"1{|}And he entered into a ship, and passed over, and came into his own city.{|}2{|}And, behold, they brought to him a man sick of the palsy, lying on a bed: and Jesus{~}seeing their faith said unto the sick of the palsy;{~}{r}Son, be of good cheer; thy sins be forgiven thee.{/r}{|}3{|}And, behold, certain of the scribes said within themselves, This man blasphemeth.{|}4{|}And Jesus knowing their thoughts said,{~}{r}Wherefore think ye evil in your hearts?{/r}{|}5{|}{r}For whether is easier, to say, Thy sins be forgiven thee; or to say, Arise, and walk?{/r}{|}6{|}{r}But that ye may know that the Son of man hath power on earth to forgive sins,{/r}{~}(then saith he to the sick of the palsy,){~}{r}Arise, take up thy bed, and go unto thine house.{/r}{|}7{|}And he arose, and departed to his house.{|}8{|}But when the multitudes saw it, they marvelled, and glorified God, which had given such{~}power unto men.{|}9{|}And as Jesus passed forth from thence, he saw a man, named Matthew, sitting at the{~}receipt of custom: and he saith unto him,{~}{r}Follow me.{/r}{~}And he arose, and followed him.{|}10{|}And it came to pass, as Jesus sat at meat in the house, behold, many publicans and{~}sinners came and sat down with him and his disciples.{|}11{|}And when the Pharisees saw it, they said unto his disciples, Why eateth your Master with{~}publicans and sinners?{|}12{|}But when Jesus heard that, he said unto them,{~}{r}They that be whole need not a physician, but they that are sick.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}But go ye and learn what that meaneth, I will have mercy, and not sacrifice: for I am{/r}{~}{r}not come to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.{/r}{|}14{|}Then came to him the disciples of John, saying, Why do we and the Pharisees fast oft,{~}but thy disciples fast not?{|}15{|}And Jesus said unto them,{~}{r}Can the children of the bridechamber mourn, as long as the bridegroom is with them? but{/r}{~}{r}the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken from them, and then shall they{/r}{~}{r}fast.{/r}{|}16{|}{r}No man putteth a piece of new cloth unto an old garment, for that which is put in to{/r}{~}{r}fill it up taketh from the garment, and the rent is made worse.{/r}{|}17{|}{r}Neither do men put new wine into old bottles: else the bottles break, and the wine{/r}{~}{r}runneth out, and the bottles perish: but they put new wine into new bottles, and both{/r}{~}{r}are preserved.{/r}{|}18{|}While he spake these things unto them, behold, there came a certain ruler, and{~}worshipped him, saying, My daughter is even now dead: but come and lay thy hand upon{~}her, and she shall live.{|}19{|}And Jesus arose, and followed him, and so did his disciples.{|}20{|}And, behold, a woman, which was diseased with an issue of blood twelve years, came{~}behind him, and touched the hem of his garment:{|}21{|}For she said within herself, If I may but touch his garment, I shall be whole.{|}22{|}But Jesus turned him about, and when he saw her, he said,{~}{r}Daughter, be of good comfort; thy faith hath made thee whole.{/r}{~}And the woman was made whole from that hour.{|}23{|}And when Jesus came into the ruler’s house, and saw the minstrels and the people making{~}a noise,{|}24{|}He said unto them,{~}{r}Give place: for the maid is not dead, but sleepeth.{/r}{~}And they laughed him to scorn.{|}25{|}But when the people were put forth, he went in, and took her by the hand, and the maid{~}arose.{|}26{|}And the fame hereof went abroad into all that land.{|}27{|}And when Jesus departed thence, two blind men followed him, crying, and saying, Thou Son{~}of David, have mercy on us.{|}28{|}And when he was come into the house, the blind men came to him: and Jesus saith unto{~}them,{~}{r}Believe ye that I am able to do this?{/r}{~}They said unto him, Yea, Lord.{|}29{|}Then touched he their eyes, saying,{~}{r}According to your faith be it unto you.{/r}{|}30{|}And their eyes were opened; and Jesus straitly charged them, saying,{~}{r}See that no man know it.{/r}{|}31{|}But they, when they were departed, spread abroad his fame in all that country.{|}32{|}As they went out, behold, they brought to him a dumb man possessed with a devil.{|}33{|}And when the devil was cast out, the dumb spake: and the multitudes marvelled, saying,{~}It was never so seen in Israel.{|}34{|}But the Pharisees said, He casteth out devils through the prince of the devils.{|}35{|}And Jesus went about all the cities and villages, teaching in their synagogues, and{~}preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing every sickness and every disease among{~}the people.{|}36{|}But when he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they{~}fainted, and were scattered abroad, as sheep having no shepherd.{|}37{|}Then saith he unto his disciples,{~}{r}The harvest truly is plenteous, but the labourers are few;{/r}{|}38{|}{r}Pray ye therefore the Lord of the harvest, that he will send forth labourers into his{/r}{~}{r}harvest.{/r}";
    case 10: return s"1{|}And when he had called unto him his twelve disciples, he gave them power against unclean{~}spirits, to cast them out, and to heal all manner of sickness and all manner of disease.{|}2{|}Now the names of the twelve apostles are these; The first, Simon, who is called Peter,{~}and Andrew his brother; James the son of Zebedee, and John his brother;{|}3{|}Philip, and Bartholomew; Thomas, and Matthew the publican; James the son of Alphaeus,{~}and Lebbaeus, whose surname was Thaddaeus;{|}4{|}Simon the Canaanite, and Judas Iscariot, who also betrayed him.{|}5{|}These twelve Jesus sent forth, and commanded them, saying,{~}{r}Go not into the way of the Gentiles, and into any city of the Samaritans enter ye not:{/r}{|}6{|}{r}But go rather to the lost sheep of the house of Israel.{/r}{|}7{|}{r}And as ye go, preach, saying, The kingdom of heaven is at hand.{/r}{|}8{|}{r}Heal the sick, cleanse the lepers, raise the dead, cast out devils: freely ye have{/r}{~}{r}received, freely give.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}Provide neither gold, nor silver, nor brass in your purses,{/r}{|}10{|}{r}Nor scrip for your journey, neither two coats, neither shoes, nor yet staves: for the{/r}{~}{r}workman is worthy of his meat.{/r}{|}11{|}{r}And into whatsoever city or town ye shall enter, enquire who in it is worthy; and there{/r}{~}{r}abide till ye go thence.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}And when ye come into an house, salute it.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}And if the house be worthy, let your peace come upon it: but if it be not worthy, let{/r}{~}{r}your peace return to you.{/r}{|}14{|}{r}And whosoever shall not receive you, nor hear your words, when ye depart out of that{/r}{~}{r}house or city, shake off the dust of your feet.{/r}{|}15{|}{r}Verily I say unto you, It shall be more tolerable for the land of Sodom and Gomorrha in{/r}{~}{r}the day of judgment, than for that city.{/r}{|}16{|}{r}Behold, I send you forth as sheep in the midst of wolves: be ye therefore wise as{/r}{~}{r}serpents, and harmless as doves.{/r}{|}17{|}{r}But beware of men: for they will deliver you up to the councils, and they will scourge{/r}{~}{r}you in their synagogues;{/r}{|}18{|}{r}And ye shall be brought before governors and kings for my sake, for a testimony against{/r}{~}{r}them and the Gentiles.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}But when they deliver you up, take no thought how or what ye shall speak: for it shall{/r}{~}{r}be given you in that same hour what ye shall speak.{/r}{|}20{|}{r}For it is not ye that speak, but the Spirit of your Father which speaketh in you.{/r}{|}21{|}{r}And the brother shall deliver up the brother to death, and the father the child: and the{/r}{~}{r}children shall rise up against their parents, and cause them to be put to death.{/r}{|}22{|}{r}And ye shall be hated of all men for my name’s sake: but he that endureth to the end{/r}{~}{r}shall be saved.{/r}{|}23{|}{r}But when they persecute you in this city, flee ye into another: for verily I say unto{/r}{~}{r}you, Ye shall not have gone over the cities of Israel, till the Son of man be come.{/r}{|}24{|}{r}The disciple is not above his master, nor the servant above his lord.{/r}{|}25{|}{r}It is enough for the disciple that he be as his master, and the servant as his lord. If{/r}{~}{r}they have called the master of the house Beelzebub, how much more shall they call them{/r}{~}{r}of his household?{/r}{|}26{|}{r}Fear them not therefore: for there is nothing covered, that shall not be revealed; and{/r}{~}{r}hid, that shall not be known.{/r}{|}27{|}{r}What I tell you in darkness, that speak ye in light: and what ye hear in the ear, that{/r}{~}{r}preach ye upon the housetops.{/r}{|}28{|}{r}And fear not them which kill the body, but are not able to kill the soul: but rather{/r}{~}{r}fear him which is able to destroy both soul and body in hell.{/r}{|}29{|}{r}Are not two sparrows sold for a farthing? and one of them shall not fall on the ground{/r}{~}{r}without your Father.{/r}{|}30{|}{r}But the very hairs of your head are all numbered.{/r}{|}31{|}{r}Fear ye not therefore, ye are of more value than many sparrows.{/r}{|}32{|}{r}Whosoever therefore shall confess me before men, him will I confess also before my{/r}{~}{r}Father which is in heaven.{/r}{|}33{|}{r}But whosoever shall deny me before men, him will I also deny before my Father which is{/r}{~}{r}in heaven.{/r}{|}34{|}{r}Think not that I am come to send peace on earth: I came not to send peace, but a sword.{/r}{|}35{|}{r}For I am come to set a man at variance against his father, and the daughter against her{/r}{~}{r}mother, and the daughter in law against her mother in law.{/r}{|}36{|}{r}And a man’s foes shall be they of his own household.{/r}{|}37{|}{r}He that loveth father or mother more than me is not worthy of me: and he that loveth son{/r}{~}{r}or daughter more than me is not worthy of me.{/r}{|}38{|}{r}And he that taketh not his cross, and followeth after me, is not worthy of me.{/r}{|}39{|}{r}He that findeth his life shall lose it: and he that loseth his life for my sake shall{/r}{~}{r}find it.{/r}{|}40{|}{r}He that receiveth you receiveth me, and he that receiveth me receiveth him that sent me.{/r}{|}41{|}{r}He that receiveth a prophet in the name of a prophet shall receive a prophet’s reward;{/r}{~}{r}and he that receiveth a righteous man in the name of a righteous man shall receive a{/r}{~}{r}righteous man’s reward.{/r}{|}42{|}{r}And whosoever shall give to drink unto one of these little ones a cup of cold water only{/r}{~}{r}in the name of a disciple, verily I say unto you, he shall in no wise lose his reward.{/r}";
    case 11: return s"1{|}And it came to pass, when Jesus had made an end of commanding his twelve disciples, he{~}departed thence to teach and to preach in their cities.{|}2{|}Now when John had heard in the prison the works of Christ, he sent two of his disciples,{|}3{|}And said unto him, Art thou he that should come, or do we look for another?{|}4{|}Jesus answered and said unto them,{~}{r}Go and shew John again those things which ye do hear and see:{/r}{|}5{|}{r}The blind receive their sight, and the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, and the deaf{/r}{~}{r}hear, the dead are raised up, and the poor have the gospel preached to them.{/r}{|}6{|}{r}And blessed is he, whosoever shall not be offended in me.{/r}{|}7{|}And as they departed, Jesus began to say unto the multitudes concerning John,{~}{r}What went ye out into the wilderness to see? A reed shaken with the wind?{/r}{|}8{|}{r}But what went ye out for to see? A man clothed in soft raiment? behold, they that wear{/r}{~}{r}soft clothing are in kings’ houses.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}But what went ye out for to see? A prophet? yea, I say unto you, and more than a{/r}{~}{r}prophet.{/r}{|}10{|}{r}For this is he, of whom it is written, Behold, I send my messenger before thy face,{/r}{~}{r}which shall prepare thy way before thee.{/r}{|}11{|}{r}Verily I say unto you, Among them that are born of women there hath not risen a greater{/r}{~}{r}than John the Baptist: notwithstanding he that is least in the kingdom of heaven is{/r}{~}{r}greater than he.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}And from the days of John the Baptist until now the kingdom of heaven suffereth{/r}{~}{r}violence, and the violent take it by force.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}For all the prophets and the law prophesied until John.{/r}{|}14{|}{r}And if ye will receive it, this is Elias, which was for to come.{/r}{|}15{|}{r}He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.{/r}{|}16{|}{r}But whereunto shall I liken this generation? It is like unto children sitting in the{/r}{~}{r}markets, and calling unto their fellows,{/r}{|}17{|}{r}And saying, We have piped unto you, and ye have not danced; we have mourned unto you,{/r}{~}{r}and ye have not lamented.{/r}{|}18{|}{r}For John came neither eating nor drinking, and they say, He hath a devil.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}The Son of man came eating and drinking, and they say, Behold a man gluttonous, and a{/r}{~}{r}winebibber, a friend of publicans and sinners. But wisdom is justified of her children.{/r}{|}20{|}Then began he to upbraid the cities wherein most of his mighty works were done, because{~}they repented not:{|}21{|}{r}Woe unto thee, Chorazin! woe unto thee, Bethsaida! for if the mighty works, which were{/r}{~}{r}done in you, had been done in Tyre and Sidon, they would have repented long ago in{/r}{~}{r}sackcloth and ashes.{/r}{|}22{|}{r}But I say unto you, It shall be more tolerable for Tyre and Sidon at the day of{/r}{~}{r}judgment, than for you.{/r}{|}23{|}{r}And thou, Capernaum, which art exalted unto heaven, shalt be brought down to hell: for{/r}{~}{r}if the mighty works, which have been done in thee, had been done in Sodom, it would have{/r}{~}{r}remained until this day.{/r}{|}24{|}{r}But I say unto you, That it shall be more tolerable for the land of Sodom in the day of{/r}{~}{r}judgment, than for thee.{/r}{|}25{|}At that time Jesus answered and said,{~}{r}I thank thee, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because thou hast hid these things{/r}{~}{r}from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them unto babes.{/r}{|}26{|}{r}Even so, Father: for so it seemed good in thy sight.{/r}{|}27{|}{r}All things are delivered unto me of my Father: and no man knoweth the Son, but the{/r}{~}{r}Father; neither knoweth any man the Father, save the Son, and he to whomsoever the Son{/r}{~}{r}will reveal him.{/r}{|}28{|}{r}Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest.{/r}{|}29{|}{r}Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall{/r}{~}{r}find rest unto your souls.{/r}{|}30{|}{r}For my yoke is easy, and my burden is light.{/r}";
    case 12: return s"1{|}At that time Jesus went on the sabbath day through the corn; and his disciples were an{~}hungred, and began to pluck the ears of corn, and to eat.{|}2{|}But when the Pharisees saw it, they said unto him, Behold, thy disciples do that which{~}is not lawful to do upon the sabbath day.{|}3{|}But he said unto them,{~}{r}Have ye not read what David did, when he was an hungred, and they that were with him;{/r}{|}4{|}{r}How he entered into the house of God, and did eat the shewbread, which was not lawful{/r}{~}{r}for him to eat, neither for them which were with him, but only for the priests?{/r}{|}5{|}{r}Or have ye not read in the law, how that on the sabbath days the priests in the temple{/r}{~}{r}profane the sabbath, and are blameless?{/r}{|}6{|}{r}But I say unto you, That in this place is one greater than the temple.{/r}{|}7{|}{r}But if ye had known what this meaneth, I will have mercy, and not sacrifice, ye would{/r}{~}{r}not have condemned the guiltless.{/r}{|}8{|}{r}For the Son of man is Lord even of the sabbath day.{/r}{|}9{|}And when he was departed thence, he went into their synagogue:{|}10{|}And, behold, there was a man which had his hand withered. And they asked him, saying, Is{~}it lawful to heal on the sabbath days? that they might accuse him.{|}11{|}And he said unto them,{~}{r}What man shall there be among you, that shall have one sheep, and if it fall into a pit{/r}{~}{r}on the sabbath day, will he not lay hold on it, and lift it out?{/r}{|}12{|}{r}How much then is a man better than a sheep? Wherefore it is lawful to do well on the{/r}{~}{r}sabbath days.{/r}{|}13{|}Then saith he to the man,{~}{r}Stretch forth thine hand.{/r}{~}And he stretched it forth; and it was restored whole, like as the other.{|}14{|}Then the Pharisees went out, and held a council against him, how they might destroy him.{|}15{|}But when Jesus knew it, he withdrew himself from thence: and great multitudes followed{~}him, and he healed them all;{|}16{|}And charged them that they should not make him known:{|}17{|}That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Esaias the prophet, saying,{|}18{|}Behold my servant, whom I have chosen; my beloved, in whom my soul is well pleased: I{~}will put my spirit upon him, and he shall shew judgment to the Gentiles.{|}19{|}He shall not strive, nor cry; neither shall any man hear his voice in the streets.{|}20{|}A bruised reed shall he not break, and smoking flax shall he not quench, till he send{~}forth judgment unto victory.{|}21{|}And in his name shall the Gentiles trust.{|}22{|}Then was brought unto him one possessed with a devil, blind, and dumb: and he healed{~}him, insomuch that the blind and dumb both spake and saw.{|}23{|}And all the people were amazed, and said, Is not this the son of David?{|}24{|}But when the Pharisees heard it, they said, This fellow doth not cast out devils, but by{~}Beelzebub the prince of the devils.{|}25{|}And Jesus knew their thoughts, and said unto them,{~}{r}Every kingdom divided against itself is brought to desolation; and every city or house{/r}{~}{r}divided against itself shall not stand:{/r}{|}26{|}{r}And if Satan cast out Satan, he is divided against himself; how shall then his kingdom{/r}{~}{r}stand?{/r}{|}27{|}{r}And if I by Beelzebub cast out devils, by whom do your children cast them out? therefore{/r}{~}{r}they shall be your judges.{/r}{|}28{|}{r}But if I cast out devils by the Spirit of God, then the kingdom of God is come unto you.{/r}{|}29{|}{r}Or else how can one enter into a strong man’s house, and spoil his goods, except he{/r}{~}{r}first bind the strong man? and then he will spoil his house.{/r}{|}30{|}{r}He that is not with me is against me; and he that gathereth not with me scattereth{/r}{~}{r}abroad.{/r}{|}31{|}{r}Wherefore I say unto you, All manner of sin and blasphemy shall be forgiven unto men:{/r}{~}{r}but the blasphemy against the Holy Ghost shall not be forgiven unto men.{/r}{|}32{|}{r}And whosoever speaketh a word against the Son of man, it shall be forgiven him: but{/r}{~}{r}whosoever speaketh against the Holy Ghost, it shall not be forgiven him, neither in this{/r}{~}{r}world, neither in the world to come.{/r}{|}33{|}{r}Either make the tree good, and his fruit good; or else make the tree corrupt, and his{/r}{~}{r}fruit corrupt: for the tree is known by his fruit.{/r}{|}34{|}{r}O generation of vipers, how can ye, being evil, speak good things? for out of the{/r}{~}{r}abundance of the heart the mouth speaketh.{/r}{|}35{|}{r}A good man out of the good treasure of the heart bringeth forth good things: and an evil{/r}{~}{r}man out of the evil treasure bringeth forth evil things.{/r}{|}36{|}{r}But I say unto you, That every idle word that men shall speak, they shall give account{/r}{~}{r}thereof in the day of judgment.{/r}{|}37{|}{r}For by thy words thou shalt be justified, and by thy words thou shalt be condemned.{/r}{|}38{|}Then certain of the scribes and of the Pharisees answered, saying, Master, we would see{~}a sign from thee.{|}39{|}But he answered and said unto them,{~}{r}An evil and adulterous generation seeketh after a sign; and there shall no sign be given{/r}{~}{r}to it, but the sign of the prophet Jonas:{/r}{|}40{|}{r}For as Jonas was three days and three nights in the whale’s belly; so shall the Son of{/r}{~}{r}man be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth.{/r}{|}41{|}{r}The men of Nineveh shall rise in judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it:{/r}{~}{r}because they repented at the preaching of Jonas; and, behold, a greater than Jonas is{/r}{~}{r}here.{/r}{|}42{|}{r}The queen of the south shall rise up in the judgment with this generation, and shall{/r}{~}{r}condemn it: for she came from the uttermost parts of the earth to hear the wisdom of{/r}{~}{r}Solomon; and, behold, a greater than Solomon is here.{/r}{|}43{|}{r}When the unclean spirit is gone out of a man, he walketh through dry places, seeking{/r}{~}{r}rest, and findeth none.{/r}{|}44{|}{r}Then he saith, I will return into my house from whence I came out; and when he is come,{/r}{~}{r}he findeth it empty, swept, and garnished.{/r}{|}45{|}{r}Then goeth he, and taketh with himself seven other spirits more wicked than himself, and{/r}{~}{r}they enter in and dwell there: and the last state of that man is worse than the first.{/r}{~}{r}Even so shall it be also unto this wicked generation.{/r}{|}46{|}While he yet talked to the people, behold, his mother and his brethren stood without,{~}desiring to speak with him.{|}47{|}Then one said unto him, Behold, thy mother and thy brethren stand without, desiring to{~}speak with thee.{|}48{|}But he answered and said unto him that told him,{~}{r}Who is my mother? and who are my brethren?{/r}{|}49{|}And he stretched forth his hand toward his disciples, and said,{~}{r}Behold my mother and my brethren!{/r}{|}50{|}{r}For whosoever shall do the will of my Father which is in heaven, the same is my brother,{/r}{~}{r}and sister, and mother.{/r}";
    case 13: return s"1{|}The same day went Jesus out of the house, and sat by the sea side.{|}2{|}And great multitudes were gathered together unto him, so that he went into a ship, and{~}sat; and the whole multitude stood on the shore.{|}3{|}And he spake many things unto them in parables, saying,{~}{r}Behold, a sower went forth to sow;{/r}{|}4{|}{r}And when he sowed, some seeds fell by the way side, and the fowls came and devoured them{/r}{~}{r}up:{/r}{|}5{|}{r}Some fell upon stony places, where they had not much earth: and forthwith they sprung{/r}{~}{r}up, because they had no deepness of earth:{/r}{|}6{|}{r}And when the sun was up, they were scorched; and because they had no root, they withered{/r}{~}{r}away.{/r}{|}7{|}{r}And some fell among thorns; and the thorns sprung up, and choked them:{/r}{|}8{|}{r}But other fell into good ground, and brought forth fruit, some an hundredfold, some{/r}{~}{r}sixtyfold, some thirtyfold.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.{/r}{|}10{|}And the disciples came, and said unto him, Why speakest thou unto them in parables?{|}11{|}He answered and said unto them,{~}{r}Because it is given unto you to know the mysteries of the kingdom of heaven, but to them{/r}{~}{r}it is not given.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}For whosoever hath, to him shall be given, and he shall have more abundance: but{/r}{~}{r}whosoever hath not, from him shall be taken away even that he hath.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}Therefore speak I to them in parables: because they seeing see not; and hearing they{/r}{~}{r}hear not, neither do they understand.{/r}{|}14{|}{r}And in them is fulfilled the prophecy of Esaias, which saith, By hearing ye shall hear,{/r}{~}{r}and shall not understand; and seeing ye shall see, and shall not perceive:{/r}{|}15{|}{r}For this people’s heart is waxed gross, and their ears are dull of hearing, and their{/r}{~}{r}eyes they have closed; lest at any time they should see with their eyes, and hear with{/r}{~}{r}their ears, and should understand with their heart, and should be converted, and I{/r}{~}{r}should heal them.{/r}{|}16{|}{r}But blessed are your eyes, for they see: and your ears, for they hear.{/r}{|}17{|}{r}For verily I say unto you, That many prophets and righteous men have desired to see{/r}{~}{r}those things which ye see, and have not seen them; and to hear those things which ye{/r}{~}{r}hear, and have not heard them.{/r}{|}18{|}{r}Hear ye therefore the parable of the sower.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}When any one heareth the word of the kingdom, and understandeth it not, then cometh the{/r}{~}{r}wicked one, and catcheth away that which was sown in his heart. This is he which{/r}{~}{r}received seed by the way side.{/r}{|}20{|}{r}But he that received the seed into stony places, the same is he that heareth the word,{/r}{~}{r}and anon with joy receiveth it;{/r}{|}21{|}{r}Yet hath he not root in himself, but dureth for a while: for when tribulation or{/r}{~}{r}persecution ariseth because of the word, by and by he is offended.{/r}{|}22{|}{r}He also that received seed among the thorns is he that heareth the word; and the care of{/r}{~}{r}this world, and the deceitfulness of riches, choke the word, and he becometh unfruitful.{/r}{|}23{|}{r}But he that received seed into the good ground is he that heareth the word, and{/r}{~}{r}understandeth it; which also beareth fruit, and bringeth forth, some an hundredfold,{/r}{~}{r}some sixty, some thirty.{/r}{|}24{|}Another parable put he forth unto them, saying,{~}{r}The kingdom of heaven is likened unto a man which sowed good seed in his field:{/r}{|}25{|}{r}But while men slept, his enemy came and sowed tares among the wheat, and went his way.{/r}{|}26{|}{r}But when the blade was sprung up, and brought forth fruit, then appeared the tares also.{/r}{|}27{|}{r}So the servants of the householder came and said unto him, Sir, didst not thou sow good{/r}{~}{r}seed in thy field? from whence then hath it tares?{/r}{|}28{|}{r}He said unto them, An enemy hath done this. The servants said unto him, Wilt thou then{/r}{~}{r}that we go and gather them up?{/r}{|}29{|}{r}But he said, Nay; lest while ye gather up the tares, ye root up also the wheat with{/r}{~}{r}them.{/r}{|}30{|}{r}Let both grow together until the harvest: and in the time of harvest I will say to the{/r}{~}{r}reapers, Gather ye together first the tares, and bind them in bundles to burn them: but{/r}{~}{r}gather the wheat into my barn.{/r}{|}31{|}Another parable put he forth unto them, saying,{~}{r}The kingdom of heaven is like to a grain of mustard seed, which a man took, and sowed in{/r}{~}{r}his field:{/r}{|}32{|}{r}Which indeed is the least of all seeds: but when it is grown, it is the greatest among{/r}{~}{r}herbs, and becometh a tree, so that the birds of the air come and lodge in the branches{/r}{~}{r}thereof.{/r}{|}33{|}Another parable spake he unto them;{~}{r}The kingdom of heaven is like unto leaven, which a woman took, and hid in three measures{/r}{~}{r}of meal, till the whole was leavened.{/r}{|}34{|}All these things spake Jesus unto the multitude in parables; and without a parable spake{~}he not unto them:{|}35{|}That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, saying, I will open my mouth{~}in parables; I will utter things which have been kept secret from the foundation of the{~}world.{|}36{|}Then Jesus sent the multitude away, and went into the house: and his disciples came unto{~}him, saying, Declare unto us the parable of the tares of the field.{|}37{|}He answered and said unto them,{~}{r}He that soweth the good seed is the Son of man;{/r}{|}38{|}{r}The field is the world; the good seed are the children of the kingdom; but the tares are{/r}{~}{r}the children of the wicked one;{/r}{|}39{|}{r}The enemy that sowed them is the devil; the harvest is the end of the world; and the{/r}{~}{r}reapers are the angels.{/r}{|}40{|}{r}As therefore the tares are gathered and burned in the fire; so shall it be in the end of{/r}{~}{r}this world.{/r}{|}41{|}{r}The Son of man shall send forth his angels, and they shall gather out of his kingdom all{/r}{~}{r}things that offend, and them which do iniquity;{/r}{|}42{|}{r}And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of{/r}{~}{r}teeth.{/r}{|}43{|}{r}Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath{/r}{~}{r}ears to hear, let him hear.{/r}{|}44{|}{r}Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto treasure hid in a field; the which when a man{/r}{~}{r}hath found, he hideth, and for joy thereof goeth and selleth all that he hath, and{/r}{~}{r}buyeth that field.{/r}{|}45{|}{r}Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto a merchant man, seeking goodly pearls:{/r}{|}46{|}{r}Who, when he had found one pearl of great price, went and sold all that he had, and{/r}{~}{r}bought it.{/r}{|}47{|}{r}Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto a net, that was cast into the sea, and{/r}{~}{r}gathered of every kind:{/r}{|}48{|}{r}Which, when it was full, they drew to shore, and sat down, and gathered the good into{/r}{~}{r}vessels, but cast the bad away.{/r}{|}49{|}{r}So shall it be at the end of the world: the angels shall come forth, and sever the{/r}{~}{r}wicked from among the just,{/r}{|}50{|}{r}And shall cast them into the furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of{/r}{~}{r}teeth.{/r}{|}51{|}Jesus saith unto them,{~}{r}Have ye understood all these things?{/r}{~}They say unto him, Yea, Lord.{|}52{|}Then said he unto them,{~}{r}Therefore every scribe which is instructed unto the kingdom of heaven is like unto a man{/r}{~}{r}that is an householder, which bringeth forth out of his treasure things new and old.{/r}{|}53{|}And it came to pass, that when Jesus had finished these parables, he departed thence.{|}54{|}And when he was come into his own country, he taught them in their synagogue, insomuch{~}that they were astonished, and said, Whence hath this man this wisdom, and these mighty{~}works?{|}55{|}Is not this the carpenter’s son? is not his mother called Mary? and his brethren, James,{~}and Joses, and Simon, and Judas?{|}56{|}And his sisters, are they not all with us? Whence then hath this man all these things?{|}57{|}And they were offended in him. But Jesus said unto them,{~}{r}A prophet is not without honour, save in his own country, and in his own house.{/r}{|}58{|}And he did not many mighty works there because of their unbelief.";
    case 14: return s"1{|}At that time Herod the tetrarch heard of the fame of Jesus,{|}2{|}And said unto his servants, This is John the Baptist; he is risen from the dead; and{~}therefore mighty works do shew forth themselves in him.{|}3{|}For Herod had laid hold on John, and bound him, and put him in prison for Herodias’{~}sake, his brother Philip’s wife.{|}4{|}For John said unto him, It is not lawful for thee to have her.{|}5{|}And when he would have put him to death, he feared the multitude, because they counted{~}him as a prophet.{|}6{|}But when Herod’s birthday was kept, the daughter of Herodias danced before them, and{~}pleased Herod.{|}7{|}Whereupon he promised with an oath to give her whatsoever she would ask.{|}8{|}And she, being before instructed of her mother, said, Give me here John Baptist’s head{~}in a charger.{|}9{|}And the king was sorry: nevertheless for the oath’s sake, and them which sat with him at{~}meat, he commanded it to be given her.{|}10{|}And he sent, and beheaded John in the prison.{|}11{|}And his head was brought in a charger, and given to the damsel: and she brought it to{~}her mother.{|}12{|}And his disciples came, and took up the body, and buried it, and went and told Jesus.{|}13{|}When Jesus heard of it, he departed thence by ship into a desert place apart: and when{~}the people had heard thereof, they followed him on foot out of the cities.{|}14{|}And Jesus went forth, and saw a great multitude, and was moved with compassion toward{~}them, and he healed their sick.{|}15{|}And when it was evening, his disciples came to him, saying, This is a desert place, and{~}the time is now past; send the multitude away, that they may go into the villages, and{~}buy themselves victuals.{|}16{|}But Jesus said unto them,{~}{r}They need not depart; give ye them to eat.{/r}{|}17{|}And they say unto him, We have here but five loaves, and two fishes.{|}18{|}He said,{~}{r}Bring them hither to me.{/r}{|}19{|}And he commanded the multitude to sit down on the grass, and took the five loaves, and{~}the two fishes, and looking up to heaven, he blessed, and brake, and gave the loaves to{~}his disciples, and the disciples to the multitude.{|}20{|}And they did all eat, and were filled: and they took up of the fragments that remained{~}twelve baskets full.{|}21{|}And they that had eaten were about five thousand men, beside women and children.{|}22{|}And straightway Jesus constrained his disciples to get into a ship, and to go before him{~}unto the other side, while he sent the multitudes away.{|}23{|}And when he had sent the multitudes away, he went up into a mountain apart to pray: and{~}when the evening was come, he was there alone.{|}24{|}But the ship was now in the midst of the sea, tossed with waves: for the wind was{~}contrary.{|}25{|}And in the fourth watch of the night Jesus went unto them, walking on the sea.{|}26{|}And when the disciples saw him walking on the sea, they were troubled, saying, It is a{~}spirit; and they cried out for fear.{|}27{|}But straightway Jesus spake unto them, saying,{~}{r}Be of good cheer; it is I; be not afraid.{/r}{|}28{|}And Peter answered him and said, Lord, if it be thou, bid me come unto thee on the{~}water.{|}29{|}And he said,{~}{r}Come.{/r}{~}And when Peter was come down out of the ship, he walked on the water, to go to Jesus.{|}30{|}But when he saw the wind boisterous, he was afraid; and beginning to sink, he cried,{~}saying, Lord, save me.{|}31{|}And immediately Jesus stretched forth his hand, and caught him, and said unto him,{~}{r}O thou of little faith, wherefore didst thou doubt?{/r}{|}32{|}And when they were come into the ship, the wind ceased.{|}33{|}Then they that were in the ship came and worshipped him, saying, Of a truth thou art the{~}Son of God.{|}34{|}And when they were gone over, they came into the land of Gennesaret.{|}35{|}And when the men of that place had knowledge of him, they sent out into all that country{~}round about, and brought unto him all that were diseased;{|}36{|}And besought him that they might only touch the hem of his garment: and as many as{~}touched were made perfectly whole.";
    case 15: return s"1{|}Then came to Jesus scribes and Pharisees, which were of Jerusalem, saying,{|}2{|}Why do thy disciples transgress the tradition of the elders? for they wash not their{~}hands when they eat bread.{|}3{|}But he answered and said unto them,{~}{r}Why do ye also transgress the commandment of God by your tradition?{/r}{|}4{|}{r}For God commanded, saying, Honour thy father and mother: and, He that curseth father or{/r}{~}{r}mother, let him die the death.{/r}{|}5{|}{r}But ye say, Whosoever shall say to his father or his mother, It is a gift, by whatsoever{/r}{~}{r}thou mightest be profited by me;{/r}{|}6{|}{r}And honour not his father or his mother, he shall be free. Thus have ye made the{/r}{~}{r}commandment of God of none effect by your tradition.{/r}{|}7{|}{r}Ye hypocrites, well did Esaias prophesy of you, saying,{/r}{|}8{|}{r}This people draweth nigh unto me with their mouth, and honoureth me with their lips; but{/r}{~}{r}their heart is far from me.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}But in vain they do worship me, teaching for doctrines the commandments of men.{/r}{|}10{|}And he called the multitude, and said unto them,{~}{r}Hear, and understand:{/r}{|}11{|}{r}Not that which goeth into the mouth defileth a man; but that which cometh out of the{/r}{~}{r}mouth, this defileth a man.{/r}{|}12{|}Then came his disciples, and said unto him, Knowest thou that the Pharisees were{~}offended, after they heard this saying?{|}13{|}But he answered and said,{~}{r}Every plant, which my heavenly Father hath not planted, shall be rooted up.{/r}{|}14{|}{r}Let them alone: they be blind leaders of the blind. And if the blind lead the blind,{/r}{~}{r}both shall fall into the ditch.{/r}{|}15{|}Then answered Peter and said unto him, Declare unto us this parable.{|}16{|}And Jesus said,{~}{r}Are ye also yet without understanding?{/r}{|}17{|}{r}Do not ye yet understand, that whatsoever entereth in at the mouth goeth into the belly,{/r}{~}{r}and is cast out into the draught?{/r}{|}18{|}{r}But those things which proceed out of the mouth come forth from the heart; and they{/r}{~}{r}defile the man.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}For out of the heart proceed evil thoughts, murders, adulteries, fornications, thefts,{/r}{~}{r}false witness, blasphemies:{/r}{|}20{|}{r}These are the things which defile a man: but to eat with unwashen hands defileth not a{/r}{~}{r}man.{/r}{|}21{|}Then Jesus went thence, and departed into the coasts of Tyre and Sidon.{|}22{|}And, behold, a woman of Canaan came out of the same coasts, and cried unto him, saying,{~}Have mercy on me, O Lord, thou Son of David; my daughter is grievously vexed with a{~}devil.{|}23{|}But he answered her not a word. And his disciples came and besought him, saying, Send{~}her away; for she crieth after us.{|}24{|}But he answered and said,{~}{r}I am not sent but unto the lost sheep of the house of Israel.{/r}{|}25{|}Then came she and worshipped him, saying, Lord, help me.{|}26{|}But he answered and said,{~}{r}It is not meet to take the children’s bread, and to cast it to dogs.{/r}{|}27{|}And she said, Truth, Lord: yet the dogs eat of the crumbs which fall from their masters’{~}table.{|}28{|}Then Jesus answered and said unto her,{~}{r}O woman, great is thy faith: be it unto thee even as thou wilt.{/r}{~}And her daughter was made whole from that very hour.{|}29{|}And Jesus departed from thence, and came nigh unto the sea of Galilee; and went up into{~}a mountain, and sat down there.{|}30{|}And great multitudes came unto him, having with them those that were lame, blind, dumb,{~}maimed, and many others, and cast them down at Jesus’ feet; and he healed them:{|}31{|}Insomuch that the multitude wondered, when they saw the dumb to speak, the maimed to be{~}whole, the lame to walk, and the blind to see: and they glorified the God of Israel.{|}32{|}Then Jesus called his disciples unto him, and said,{~}{r}I have compassion on the multitude, because they continue with me now three days, and{/r}{~}{r}have nothing to eat: and I will not send them away fasting, lest they faint in the way.{/r}{|}33{|}And his disciples say unto him, Whence should we have so much bread in the wilderness,{~}as to fill so great a multitude?{|}34{|}And Jesus saith unto them,{~}{r}How many loaves have ye?{/r}{~}And they said, Seven, and a few little fishes.{|}35{|}And he commanded the multitude to sit down on the ground.{|}36{|}And he took the seven loaves and the fishes, and gave thanks, and brake them, and gave{~}to his disciples, and the disciples to the multitude.{|}37{|}And they did all eat, and were filled: and they took up of the broken meat that was left{~}seven baskets full.{|}38{|}And they that did eat were four thousand men, beside women and children.{|}39{|}And he sent away the multitude, and took ship, and came into the coasts of Magdala.";
    case 16: return s"1{|}The Pharisees also with the Sadducees came, and tempting desired him that he would shew{~}them a sign from heaven.{|}2{|}He answered and said unto them,{~}{r}When it is evening, ye say, It will be fair weather: for the sky is red.{/r}{|}3{|}{r}And in the morning, It will be foul weather to day: for the sky is red and lowring. O ye{/r}{~}{r}hypocrites, ye can discern the face of the sky; but can ye not discern the signs of the{/r}{~}{r}times?{/r}{|}4{|}{r}A wicked and adulterous generation seeketh after a sign; and there shall no sign be{/r}{~}{r}given unto it, but the sign of the prophet Jonas.{/r}{~}And he left them, and departed.{|}5{|}And when his disciples were come to the other side, they had forgotten to take bread.{|}6{|}Then Jesus said unto them,{~}{r}Take heed and beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees.{/r}{|}7{|}And they reasoned among themselves, saying, It is because we have taken no bread.{|}8{|}Which when Jesus perceived, he said unto them,{~}{r}O ye of little faith, why reason ye among yourselves, because ye have brought no bread?{/r}{|}9{|}{r}Do ye not yet understand, neither remember the five loaves of the five thousand, and how{/r}{~}{r}many baskets ye took up?{/r}{|}10{|}{r}Neither the seven loaves of the four thousand, and how many baskets ye took up?{/r}{|}11{|}{r}How is it that ye do not understand that I spake it not to you concerning bread, that ye{/r}{~}{r}should beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees?{/r}{|}12{|}Then understood they how that he bade them not beware of the leaven of bread, but of the{~}doctrine of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees.{|}13{|}When Jesus came into the coasts of Caesarea Philippi, he asked his disciples, saying,{~}{r}Whom do men say that I the Son of man am?{/r}{|}14{|}And they said, Some say that thou art John the Baptist: some, Elias; and others,{~}Jeremias, or one of the prophets.{|}15{|}He saith unto them,{~}{r}But whom say ye that I am?{/r}{|}16{|}And Simon Peter answered and said, Thou art the Christ, the Son of the living God.{|}17{|}And Jesus answered and said unto him,{~}{r}Blessed art thou, Simon Bar-jona: for flesh and blood hath not revealed it unto thee,{/r}{~}{r}but my Father which is in heaven.{/r}{|}18{|}{r}And I say also unto thee, That thou art Peter, and upon this rock I will build my{/r}{~}{r}church; and the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}And I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven: and whatsoever thou shalt{/r}{~}{r}bind on earth shall be bound in heaven: and whatsoever thou shalt loose on earth shall{/r}{~}{r}be loosed in heaven.{/r}{|}20{|}Then charged he his disciples that they should tell no man that he was Jesus the Christ.{|}21{|}From that time forth began Jesus to shew unto his disciples, how that he must go unto{~}Jerusalem, and suffer many things of the elders and chief priests and scribes, and be{~}killed, and be raised again the third day.{|}22{|}Then Peter took him, and began to rebuke him, saying, Be it far from thee, Lord: this{~}shall not be unto thee.{|}23{|}But he turned, and said unto Peter,{~}{r}Get thee behind me, Satan: thou art an offence unto me: for thou savourest not the{/r}{~}{r}things that be of God, but those that be of men.{/r}{|}24{|}Then said Jesus unto his disciples,{~}{r}If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow{/r}{~}{r}me.{/r}{|}25{|}{r}For whosoever will save his life shall lose it: and whosoever will lose his life for my{/r}{~}{r}sake shall find it.{/r}{|}26{|}{r}For what is a man profited, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul? or{/r}{~}{r}what shall a man give in exchange for his soul?{/r}{|}27{|}{r}For the Son of man shall come in the glory of his Father with his angels; and then he{/r}{~}{r}shall reward every man according to his works.{/r}{|}28{|}{r}Verily I say unto you, There be some standing here, which shall not taste of death, till{/r}{~}{r}they see the Son of man coming in his kingdom.{/r}";
    case 17: return s"1{|}And after six days Jesus taketh Peter, James, and John his brother, and bringeth them up{~}into an high mountain apart,{|}2{|}And was transfigured before them: and his face did shine as the sun, and his raiment was{~}white as the light.{|}3{|}And, behold, there appeared unto them Moses and Elias talking with him.{|}4{|}Then answered Peter, and said unto Jesus, Lord, it is good for us to be here: if thou{~}wilt, let us make here three tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for{~}Elias.{|}5{|}While he yet spake, behold, a bright cloud overshadowed them: and behold a voice out of{~}the cloud, which said, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased; hear ye him.{|}6{|}And when the disciples heard it, they fell on their face, and were sore afraid.{|}7{|}And Jesus came and touched them, and said,{~}{r}Arise, and be not afraid.{/r}{|}8{|}And when they had lifted up their eyes, they saw no man, save Jesus only.{|}9{|}And as they came down from the mountain, Jesus charged them, saying,{~}{r}Tell the vision to no man, until the Son of man be risen again from the dead.{/r}{|}10{|}And his disciples asked him, saying, Why then say the scribes that Elias must first{~}come?{|}11{|}And Jesus answered and said unto them,{~}{r}Elias truly shall first come, and restore all things.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}But I say unto you, That Elias is come already, and they knew him not, but have done{/r}{~}{r}unto him whatsoever they listed. Likewise shall also the Son of man suffer of them.{/r}{|}13{|}Then the disciples understood that he spake unto them of John the Baptist.{|}14{|}And when they were come to the multitude, there came to him a certain man, kneeling down{~}to him, and saying,{|}15{|}Lord, have mercy on my son: for he is lunatick, and sore vexed: for ofttimes he falleth{~}into the fire, and oft into the water.{|}16{|}And I brought him to thy disciples, and they could not cure him.{|}17{|}Then Jesus answered and said,{~}{r}O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you? how long shall I{/r}{~}{r}suffer you? bring him hither to me.{/r}{|}18{|}And Jesus rebuked the devil; and he departed out of him: and the child was cured from{~}that very hour.{|}19{|}Then came the disciples to Jesus apart, and said, Why could not we cast him out?{|}20{|}And Jesus said unto them,{~}{r}Because of your unbelief: for verily I say unto you, If ye have faith as a grain of{/r}{~}{r}mustard seed, ye shall say unto this mountain, Remove hence to yonder place; and it{/r}{~}{r}shall remove; and nothing shall be impossible unto you.{/r}{|}21{|}{r}Howbeit this kind goeth not out but by prayer and fasting.{/r}{|}22{|}And while they abode in Galilee, Jesus said unto them,{~}{r}The Son of man shall be betrayed into the hands of men:{/r}{|}23{|}{r}And they shall kill him, and the third day he shall be raised again.{/r}{~}And they were exceeding sorry.{|}24{|}And when they were come to Capernaum, they that received tribute money came to Peter,{~}and said, Doth not your master pay tribute?{|}25{|}He saith, Yes. And when he was come into the house, Jesus prevented him, saying,{~}{r}What thinkest thou, Simon? of whom do the kings of the earth take custom or tribute? of{/r}{~}{r}their own children, or of strangers?{/r}{|}26{|}Peter saith unto him, Of strangers. Jesus saith unto him,{~}{r}Then are the children free.{/r}{|}27{|}{r}Notwithstanding, lest we should offend them, go thou to the sea, and cast an hook, and{/r}{~}{r}take up the fish that first cometh up; and when thou hast opened his mouth, thou shalt{/r}{~}{r}find a piece of money: that take, and give unto them for me and thee.{/r}";
    case 18: return s"1{|}At the same time came the disciples unto Jesus, saying, Who is the greatest in the{~}kingdom of heaven?{|}2{|}And Jesus called a little child unto him, and set him in the midst of them,{|}3{|}And said,{~}{r}Verily I say unto you, Except ye be converted, and become as little children, ye shall{/r}{~}{r}not enter into the kingdom of heaven.{/r}{|}4{|}{r}Whosoever therefore shall humble himself as this little child, the same is greatest in{/r}{~}{r}the kingdom of heaven.{/r}{|}5{|}{r}And whoso shall receive one such little child in my name receiveth me.{/r}{|}6{|}{r}But whoso shall offend one of these little ones which believe in me, it were better for{/r}{~}{r}him that a millstone were hanged about his neck, and that he were drowned in the depth{/r}{~}{r}of the sea.{/r}{|}7{|}{r}Woe unto the world because of offences! for it must needs be that offences come; but woe{/r}{~}{r}to that man by whom the offence cometh!{/r}{|}8{|}{r}Wherefore if thy hand or thy foot offend thee, cut them off, and cast them from thee: it{/r}{~}{r}is better for thee to enter into life halt or maimed, rather than having two hands or{/r}{~}{r}two feet to be cast into everlasting fire.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}And if thine eye offend thee, pluck it out, and cast it from thee: it is better for thee{/r}{~}{r}to enter into life with one eye, rather than having two eyes to be cast into hell fire.{/r}{|}10{|}{r}Take heed that ye despise not one of these little ones; for I say unto you, That in{/r}{~}{r}heaven their angels do always behold the face of my Father which is in heaven.{/r}{|}11{|}{r}For the Son of man is come to save that which was lost.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}How think ye? if a man have an hundred sheep, and one of them be gone astray, doth he{/r}{~}{r}not leave the ninety and nine, and goeth into the mountains, and seeketh that which is{/r}{~}{r}gone astray?{/r}{|}13{|}{r}And if so be that he find it, verily I say unto you, he rejoiceth more of that sheep,{/r}{~}{r}than of the ninety and nine which went not astray.{/r}{|}14{|}{r}Even so it is not the will of your Father which is in heaven, that one of these little{/r}{~}{r}ones should perish.{/r}{|}15{|}{r}Moreover if thy brother shall trespass against thee, go and tell him his fault between{/r}{~}{r}thee and him alone: if he shall hear thee, thou hast gained thy brother.{/r}{|}16{|}{r}But if he will not hear thee, then take with thee one or two more, that in the mouth of{/r}{~}{r}two or three witnesses every word may be established.{/r}{|}17{|}{r}And if he shall neglect to hear them, tell it unto the church: but if he neglect to hear{/r}{~}{r}the church, let him be unto thee as an heathen man and a publican.{/r}{|}18{|}{r}Verily I say unto you, Whatsoever ye shall bind on earth shall be bound in heaven: and{/r}{~}{r}whatsoever ye shall loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}Again I say unto you, That if two of you shall agree on earth as touching any thing that{/r}{~}{r}they shall ask, it shall be done for them of my Father which is in heaven.{/r}{|}20{|}{r}For where two or three are gathered together in my name, there am I in the midst of{/r}{~}{r}them.{/r}{|}21{|}Then came Peter to him, and said, Lord, how oft shall my brother sin against me, and I{~}forgive him? till seven times?{|}22{|}Jesus saith unto him,{~}{r}I say not unto thee, Until seven times: but, Until seventy times seven.{/r}{|}23{|}{r}Therefore is the kingdom of heaven likened unto a certain king, which would take account{/r}{~}{r}of his servants.{/r}{|}24{|}{r}And when he had begun to reckon, one was brought unto him, which owed him ten thousand{/r}{~}{r}talents.{/r}{|}25{|}{r}But forasmuch as he had not to pay, his lord commanded him to be sold, and his wife, and{/r}{~}{r}children, and all that he had, and payment to be made.{/r}{|}26{|}{r}The servant therefore fell down, and worshipped him, saying, Lord, have patience with{/r}{~}{r}me, and I will pay thee all.{/r}{|}27{|}{r}Then the lord of that servant was moved with compassion, and loosed him, and forgave him{/r}{~}{r}the debt.{/r}{|}28{|}{r}But the same servant went out, and found one of his fellowservants, which owed him an{/r}{~}{r}hundred pence: and he laid hands on him, and took him by the throat, saying, Pay me that{/r}{~}{r}thou owest.{/r}{|}29{|}{r}And his fellowservant fell down at his feet, and besought him, saying, Have patience{/r}{~}{r}with me, and I will pay thee all.{/r}{|}30{|}{r}And he would not: but went and cast him into prison, till he should pay the debt.{/r}{|}31{|}{r}So when his fellowservants saw what was done, they were very sorry, and came and told{/r}{~}{r}unto their lord all that was done.{/r}{|}32{|}{r}Then his lord, after that he had called him, said unto him, O thou wicked servant, I{/r}{~}{r}forgave thee all that debt, because thou desiredst me:{/r}{|}33{|}{r}Shouldest not thou also have had compassion on thy fellowservant, even as I had pity on{/r}{~}{r}thee?{/r}{|}34{|}{r}And his lord was wroth, and delivered him to the tormentors, till he should pay all that{/r}{~}{r}was due unto him.{/r}{|}35{|}{r}So likewise shall my heavenly Father do also unto you, if ye from your hearts forgive{/r}{~}{r}not every one his brother their trespasses.{/r}";
    case 19: return s"1{|}And it came to pass, that when Jesus had finished these sayings, he departed from{~}Galilee, and came into the coasts of Judaea beyond Jordan;{|}2{|}And great multitudes followed him; and he healed them there.{|}3{|}The Pharisees also came unto him, tempting him, and saying unto him, Is it lawful for a{~}man to put away his wife for every cause?{|}4{|}And he answered and said unto them,{~}{r}Have ye not read, that he which made them at the beginning made them male and female,{/r}{|}5{|}{r}And said, For this cause shall a man leave father and mother, and shall cleave to his{/r}{~}{r}wife: and they twain shall be one flesh?{/r}{|}6{|}{r}Wherefore they are no more twain, but one flesh. What therefore God hath joined{/r}{~}{r}together, let not man put asunder.{/r}{|}7{|}They say unto him, Why did Moses then command to give a writing of divorcement, and to{~}put her away?{|}8{|}He saith unto them,{~}{r}Moses because of the hardness of your hearts suffered you to put away your wives: but{/r}{~}{r}from the beginning it was not so.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}And I say unto you, Whosoever shall put away his wife, except it be for fornication, and{/r}{~}{r}shall marry another, committeth adultery: and whoso marrieth her which is put away doth{/r}{~}{r}commit adultery.{/r}{|}10{|}His disciples say unto him, If the case of the man be so with his wife, it is not good{~}to marry.{|}11{|}But he said unto them,{~}{r}All men cannot receive this saying, save they to whom it is given.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}For there are some eunuchs, which were so born from their mother’s womb: and there are{/r}{~}{r}some eunuchs, which were made eunuchs of men: and there be eunuchs, which have made{/r}{~}{r}themselves eunuchs for the kingdom of heaven’s sake. He that is able to receive it, let{/r}{~}{r}him receive it.{/r}{|}13{|}Then were there brought unto him little children, that he should put his hands on them,{~}and pray: and the disciples rebuked them.{|}14{|}But Jesus said,{~}{r}Suffer little children, and forbid them not, to come unto me: for of such is the kingdom{/r}{~}{r}of heaven.{/r}{|}15{|}And he laid his hands on them, and departed thence.{|}16{|}And, behold, one came and said unto him, Good Master, what good thing shall I do, that I{~}may have eternal life?{|}17{|}And he said unto him,{~}{r}Why callest thou me good? there is none good but one, that is, God: but if thou wilt{/r}{~}{r}enter into life, keep the commandments.{/r}{|}18{|}He saith unto him, Which? Jesus said,{~}{r}Thou shalt do no murder, Thou shalt not commit adultery, Thou shalt not steal, Thou{/r}{~}{r}shalt not bear false witness,{/r}{|}19{|}{r}Honour thy father and thy mother: and, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.{/r}{|}20{|}The young man saith unto him, All these things have I kept from my youth up: what lack I{~}yet?{|}21{|}Jesus said unto him,{~}{r}If thou wilt be perfect, go and sell that thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou{/r}{~}{r}shalt have treasure in heaven: and come and follow me.{/r}{|}22{|}But when the young man heard that saying, he went away sorrowful: for he had great{~}possessions.{|}23{|}Then said Jesus unto his disciples,{~}{r}Verily I say unto you, That a rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom of heaven.{/r}{|}24{|}{r}And again I say unto you, It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle,{/r}{~}{r}than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God.{/r}{|}25{|}When his disciples heard it, they were exceedingly amazed, saying, Who then can be{~}saved?{|}26{|}But Jesus beheld them, and said unto them,{~}{r}With men this is impossible; but with God all things are possible.{/r}{|}27{|}Then answered Peter and said unto him, Behold, we have forsaken all, and followed thee;{~}what shall we have therefore?{|}28{|}And Jesus said unto them,{~}{r}Verily I say unto you, That ye which have followed me, in the regeneration when the Son{/r}{~}{r}of man shall sit in the throne of his glory, ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones,{/r}{~}{r}judging the twelve tribes of Israel.{/r}{|}29{|}{r}And every one that hath forsaken houses, or brethren, or sisters, or father, or mother,{/r}{~}{r}or wife, or children, or lands, for my name’s sake, shall receive an hundredfold, and{/r}{~}{r}shall inherit everlasting life.{/r}{|}30{|}{r}But many that are first shall be last; and the last shall be first.{/r}";
    case 20: return s"1{|}{r}For the kingdom of heaven is like unto a man that is an householder, which went out{/r}{~}{r}early in the morning to hire labourers into his vineyard.{/r}{|}2{|}{r}And when he had agreed with the labourers for a penny a day, he sent them into his{/r}{~}{r}vineyard.{/r}{|}3{|}{r}And he went out about the third hour, and saw others standing idle in the marketplace,{/r}{|}4{|}{r}And said unto them; Go ye also into the vineyard, and whatsoever is right I will give{/r}{~}{r}you. And they went their way.{/r}{|}5{|}{r}Again he went out about the sixth and ninth hour, and did likewise.{/r}{|}6{|}{r}And about the eleventh hour he went out, and found others standing idle, and saith unto{/r}{~}{r}them, Why stand ye here all the day idle?{/r}{|}7{|}{r}They say unto him, Because no man hath hired us. He saith unto them, Go ye also into the{/r}{~}{r}vineyard; and whatsoever is right, that shall ye receive.{/r}{|}8{|}{r}So when even was come, the lord of the vineyard saith unto his steward, Call the{/r}{~}{r}labourers, and give them their hire, beginning from the last unto the first.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}And when they came that were hired about the eleventh hour, they received every man a{/r}{~}{r}penny.{/r}{|}10{|}{r}But when the first came, they supposed that they should have received more; and they{/r}{~}{r}likewise received every man a penny.{/r}{|}11{|}{r}And when they had received it, they murmured against the goodman of the house,{/r}{|}12{|}{r}Saying, These last have wrought but one hour, and thou hast made them equal unto us,{/r}{~}{r}which have borne the burden and heat of the day.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}But he answered one of them, and said, Friend, I do thee no wrong: didst not thou agree{/r}{~}{r}with me for a penny?{/r}{|}14{|}{r}Take that thine is, and go thy way: I will give unto this last, even as unto thee.{/r}{|}15{|}{r}Is it not lawful for me to do what I will with mine own? Is thine eye evil, because I am{/r}{~}{r}good?{/r}{|}16{|}{r}So the last shall be first, and the first last: for many be called, but few chosen.{/r}{|}17{|}And Jesus going up to Jerusalem took the twelve disciples apart in the way, and said{~}unto them,{|}18{|}{r}Behold, we go up to Jerusalem; and the Son of man shall be betrayed unto the chief{/r}{~}{r}priests and unto the scribes, and they shall condemn him to death,{/r}{|}19{|}{r}And shall deliver him to the Gentiles to mock, and to scourge, and to crucify him: and{/r}{~}{r}the third day he shall rise again.{/r}{|}20{|}Then came to him the mother of Zebedee’s children with her sons, worshipping him, and{~}desiring a certain thing of him.{|}21{|}And he said unto her,{~}{r}What wilt thou?{/r}{~}She saith unto him, Grant that these my two sons may sit, the one on thy right hand, and{~}the other on the left, in thy kingdom.{|}22{|}But Jesus answered and said,{~}{r}Ye know not what ye ask. Are ye able to drink of the cup that I shall drink of, and to{/r}{~}{r}be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with?{/r}{~}They say unto him, We are able.{|}23{|}And he saith unto them,{~}{r}Ye shall drink indeed of my cup, and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized{/r}{~}{r}with: but to sit on my right hand, and on my left, is not mine to give, but it shall be{/r}{~}{r}given to them for whom it is prepared of my Father.{/r}{|}24{|}And when the ten heard it, they were moved with indignation against the two brethren.{|}25{|}But Jesus called them unto him, and said,{~}{r}Ye know that the princes of the Gentiles exercise dominion over them, and they that are{/r}{~}{r}great exercise authority upon them.{/r}{|}26{|}{r}But it shall not be so among you: but whosoever will be great among you, let him be your{/r}{~}{r}minister;{/r}{|}27{|}{r}And whosoever will be chief among you, let him be your servant:{/r}{|}28{|}{r}Even as the Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his{/r}{~}{r}life a ransom for many.{/r}{|}29{|}And as they departed from Jericho, a great multitude followed him.{|}30{|}And, behold, two blind men sitting by the way side, when they heard that Jesus passed{~}by, cried out, saying, Have mercy on us, O Lord, thou Son of David.{|}31{|}And the multitude rebuked them, because they should hold their peace: but they cried the{~}more, saying, Have mercy on us, O Lord, thou Son of David.{|}32{|}And Jesus stood still, and called them, and said,{~}{r}What will ye that I shall do unto you?{/r}{|}33{|}They say unto him, Lord, that our eyes may be opened.{|}34{|}So Jesus had compassion on them, and touched their eyes: and immediately their eyes{~}received sight, and they followed him.";
    case 21: return s"1{|}And when they drew nigh unto Jerusalem, and were come to Bethphage, unto the mount of{~}Olives, then sent Jesus two disciples,{|}2{|}Saying unto them,{~}{r}Go into the village over against you, and straightway ye shall find an ass tied, and a{/r}{~}{r}colt with her: loose them, and bring them unto me.{/r}{|}3{|}{r}And if any man say ought unto you, ye shall say, The Lord hath need of them; and{/r}{~}{r}straightway he will send them.{/r}{|}4{|}All this was done, that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, saying,{|}5{|}Tell ye the daughter of Sion, Behold, thy King cometh unto thee, meek, and sitting upon{~}an ass, and a colt the foal of an ass.{|}6{|}And the disciples went, and did as Jesus commanded them,{|}7{|}And brought the ass, and the colt, and put on them their clothes, and they set him{~}thereon.{|}8{|}And a very great multitude spread their garments in the way; others cut down branches{~}from the trees, and strawed them in the way.{|}9{|}And the multitudes that went before, and that followed, cried, saying, Hosanna to the{~}Son of David: Blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord; Hosanna in the highest.{|}10{|}And when he was come into Jerusalem, all the city was moved, saying, Who is this?{|}11{|}And the multitude said, This is Jesus the prophet of Nazareth of Galilee.{|}12{|}And Jesus went into the temple of God, and cast out all them that sold and bought in the{~}temple, and overthrew the tables of the moneychangers, and the seats of them that sold{~}doves,{|}13{|}And said unto them,{~}{r}It is written, My house shall be called the house of prayer; but ye have made it a den{/r}{~}{r}of thieves.{/r}{|}14{|}And the blind and the lame came to him in the temple; and he healed them.{|}15{|}And when the chief priests and scribes saw the wonderful things that he did, and the{~}children crying in the temple, and saying, Hosanna to the Son of David; they were sore{~}displeased,{|}16{|}And said unto him, Hearest thou what these say? And Jesus saith unto them,{~}{r}Yea; have ye never read, Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings thou hast perfected{/r}{~}{r}praise?{/r}{|}17{|}And he left them, and went out of the city into Bethany; and he lodged there.{|}18{|}Now in the morning as he returned into the city, he hungered.{|}19{|}And when he saw a fig tree in the way, he came to it, and found nothing thereon, but{~}leaves only, and said unto it,{~}{r}Let no fruit grow on thee henceforward for ever.{/r}{~}And presently the fig tree withered away.{|}20{|}And when the disciples saw it, they marvelled, saying, How soon is the fig tree withered{~}away!{|}21{|}Jesus answered and said unto them,{~}{r}Verily I say unto you, If ye have faith, and doubt not, ye shall not only do this which{/r}{~}{r}is done to the fig tree, but also if ye shall say unto this mountain, Be thou removed,{/r}{~}{r}and be thou cast into the sea; it shall be done.{/r}{|}22{|}{r}And all things, whatsoever ye shall ask in prayer, believing, ye shall receive.{/r}{|}23{|}And when he was come into the temple, the chief priests and the elders of the people{~}came unto him as he was teaching, and said, By what authority doest thou these things?{~}and who gave thee this authority?{|}24{|}And Jesus answered and said unto them,{~}{r}I also will ask you one thing, which if ye tell me, I in like wise will tell you by what{/r}{~}{r}authority I do these things.{/r}{|}25{|}{r}The baptism of John, whence was it? from heaven, or of men?{/r}{~}And they reasoned with themselves, saying, If we shall say, From heaven; he will say{~}unto us, Why did ye not then believe him?{|}26{|}But if we shall say, Of men; we fear the people; for all hold John as a prophet.{|}27{|}And they answered Jesus, and said, We cannot tell. And he said unto them,{~}{r}Neither tell I you by what authority I do these things.{/r}{|}28{|}{r}But what think ye? A certain man had two sons; and he came to the first, and said, Son,{/r}{~}{r}go work to day in my vineyard.{/r}{|}29{|}{r}He answered and said, I will not: but afterward he repented, and went.{/r}{|}30{|}{r}And he came to the second, and said likewise. And he answered and said, I go, sir: and{/r}{~}{r}went not.{/r}{|}31{|}{r}Whether of them twain did the will of his father?{/r}{~}They say unto him, The first. Jesus saith unto them,{~}{r}Verily I say unto you, That the publicans and the harlots go into the kingdom of God{/r}{~}{r}before you.{/r}{|}32{|}{r}For John came unto you in the way of righteousness, and ye believed him not: but the{/r}{~}{r}publicans and the harlots believed him: and ye, when ye had seen it, repented not{/r}{~}{r}afterward, that ye might believe him.{/r}{|}33{|}{r}Hear another parable: There was a certain householder, which planted a vineyard, and{/r}{~}{r}hedged it round about, and digged a winepress in it, and built a tower, and let it out{/r}{~}{r}to husbandmen, and went into a far country:{/r}{|}34{|}{r}And when the time of the fruit drew near, he sent his servants to the husbandmen, that{/r}{~}{r}they might receive the fruits of it.{/r}{|}35{|}{r}And the husbandmen took his servants, and beat one, and killed another, and stoned{/r}{~}{r}another.{/r}{|}36{|}{r}Again, he sent other servants more than the first: and they did unto them likewise.{/r}{|}37{|}{r}But last of all he sent unto them his son, saying, They will reverence my son.{/r}{|}38{|}{r}But when the husbandmen saw the son, they said among themselves, This is the heir; come,{/r}{~}{r}let us kill him, and let us seize on his inheritance.{/r}{|}39{|}{r}And they caught him, and cast him out of the vineyard, and slew him.{/r}{|}40{|}{r}When the lord therefore of the vineyard cometh, what will he do unto those husbandmen?{/r}{|}41{|}They say unto him, He will miserably destroy those wicked men, and will let out his{~}vineyard unto other husbandmen, which shall render him the fruits in their seasons.{|}42{|}Jesus saith unto them,{~}{r}Did ye never read in the scriptures, The stone which the builders rejected, the same is{/r}{~}{r}become the head of the corner: this is the Lord’s doing, and it is marvellous in our{/r}{~}{r}eyes?{/r}{|}43{|}{r}Therefore say I unto you, The kingdom of God shall be taken from you, and given to a{/r}{~}{r}nation bringing forth the fruits thereof.{/r}{|}44{|}{r}And whosoever shall fall on this stone shall be broken: but on whomsoever it shall fall,{/r}{~}{r}it will grind him to powder.{/r}{|}45{|}And when the chief priests and Pharisees had heard his parables, they perceived that he{~}spake of them.{|}46{|}But when they sought to lay hands on him, they feared the multitude, because they took{~}him for a prophet.";
    case 22: return s"1{|}And Jesus answered and spake unto them again by parables, and said,{|}2{|}{r}The kingdom of heaven is like unto a certain king, which made a marriage for his son,{/r}{|}3{|}{r}And sent forth his servants to call them that were bidden to the wedding: and they would{/r}{~}{r}not come.{/r}{|}4{|}{r}Again, he sent forth other servants, saying, Tell them which are bidden, Behold, I have{/r}{~}{r}prepared my dinner: my oxen and my fatlings are killed, and all things are ready: come{/r}{~}{r}unto the marriage.{/r}{|}5{|}{r}But they made light of it, and went their ways, one to his farm, another to his{/r}{~}{r}merchandise:{/r}{|}6{|}{r}And the remnant took his servants, and entreated them spitefully, and slew them.{/r}{|}7{|}{r}But when the king heard thereof, he was wroth: and he sent forth his armies, and{/r}{~}{r}destroyed those murderers, and burned up their city.{/r}{|}8{|}{r}Then saith he to his servants, The wedding is ready, but they which were bidden were not{/r}{~}{r}worthy.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}Go ye therefore into the highways, and as many as ye shall find, bid to the marriage.{/r}{|}10{|}{r}So those servants went out into the highways, and gathered together all as many as they{/r}{~}{r}found, both bad and good: and the wedding was furnished with guests.{/r}{|}11{|}{r}And when the king came in to see the guests, he saw there a man which had not on a{/r}{~}{r}wedding garment:{/r}{|}12{|}{r}And he saith unto him, Friend, how camest thou in hither not having a wedding garment?{/r}{~}{r}And he was speechless.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}Then said the king to the servants, Bind him hand and foot, and take him away, and cast{/r}{~}{r}him into outer darkness; there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.{/r}{|}14{|}{r}For many are called, but few are chosen.{/r}{|}15{|}Then went the Pharisees, and took counsel how they might entangle him in his talk.{|}16{|}And they sent out unto him their disciples with the Herodians, saying, Master, we know{~}that thou art true, and teachest the way of God in truth, neither carest thou for any{~}man: for thou regardest not the person of men.{|}17{|}Tell us therefore, What thinkest thou? Is it lawful to give tribute unto Caesar, or not?{|}18{|}But Jesus perceived their wickedness, and said,{~}{r}Why tempt ye me, ye hypocrites?{/r}{|}19{|}{r}Shew me the tribute money.{/r}{~}And they brought unto him a penny.{|}20{|}And he saith unto them,{~}{r}Whose is this image and superscription?{/r}{|}21{|}They say unto him, Cæsar’s. Then saith he unto them,{~}{r}Render therefore unto Cæsar the things which are Cæsar’s; and unto God the things that{/r}{~}{r}are God’s.{/r}{|}22{|}When they had heard these words, they marvelled, and left him, and went their way.{|}23{|}The same day came to him the Sadducees, which say that there is no resurrection, and{~}asked him,{|}24{|}Saying, Master, Moses said, If a man die, having no children, his brother shall marry{~}his wife, and raise up seed unto his brother.{|}25{|}Now there were with us seven brethren: and the first, when he had married a wife,{~}deceased, and, having no issue, left his wife unto his brother:{|}26{|}Likewise the second also, and the third, unto the seventh.{|}27{|}And last of all the woman died also.{|}28{|}Therefore in the resurrection whose wife shall she be of the seven? for they all had{~}her.{|}29{|}Jesus answered and said unto them,{~}{r}Ye do err, not knowing the scriptures, nor the power of God.{/r}{|}30{|}{r}For in the resurrection they neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as the{/r}{~}{r}angels of God in heaven.{/r}{|}31{|}{r}But as touching the resurrection of the dead, have ye not read that which was spoken{/r}{~}{r}unto you by God, saying,{/r}{|}32{|}{r}I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob? God is not the God{/r}{~}{r}of the dead, but of the living.{/r}{|}33{|}And when the multitude heard this, they were astonished at his doctrine.{|}34{|}But when the Pharisees had heard that he had put the Sadducees to silence, they were{~}gathered together.{|}35{|}Then one of them, which was a lawyer, asked him a question, tempting him, and saying,{|}36{|}Master, which is the great commandment in the law?{|}37{|}Jesus said unto him,{~}{r}Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all{/r}{~}{r}thy mind.{/r}{|}38{|}{r}This is the first and great commandment.{/r}{|}39{|}{r}And the second is like unto it, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.{/r}{|}40{|}{r}On these two commandments hang all the law and the prophets.{/r}{|}41{|}While the Pharisees were gathered together, Jesus asked them,{|}42{|}Saying,{~}{r}What think ye of Christ? whose son is he?{/r}{~}They say unto him, The Son of David.{|}43{|}He saith unto them,{~}{r}How then doth David in spirit call him Lord, saying,{/r}{|}44{|}{r}The LORD said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy{/r}{~}{r}footstool?{/r}{|}45{|}{r}If David then call him Lord, how is he his son?{/r}{|}46{|}And no man was able to answer him a word, neither durst any man from that day forth ask{~}him any more questions.";
    case 23: return s"1{|}Then spake Jesus to the multitude, and to his disciples,{|}2{|}Saying,{~}{r}The scribes and the Pharisees sit in Moses’ seat:{/r}{|}3{|}{r}All therefore whatsoever they bid you observe, that observe and do; but do not ye after{/r}{~}{r}their works: for they say, and do not.{/r}{|}4{|}{r}For they bind heavy burdens and grievous to be borne, and lay them on men’s shoulders;{/r}{~}{r}but they themselves will not move them with one of their fingers.{/r}{|}5{|}{r}But all their works they do for to be seen of men: they make broad their phylacteries,{/r}{~}{r}and enlarge the borders of their garments,{/r}{|}6{|}{r}And love the uppermost rooms at feasts, and the chief seats in the synagogues,{/r}{|}7{|}{r}And greetings in the markets, and to be called of men, Rabbi, Rabbi.{/r}{|}8{|}{r}But be not ye called Rabbi: for one is your Master, even Christ; and all ye are{/r}{~}{r}brethren.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}And call no man your father upon the earth: for one is your Father, which is in heaven.{/r}{|}10{|}{r}Neither be ye called masters: for one is your Master, even Christ.{/r}{|}11{|}{r}But he that is greatest among you shall be your servant.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}And whosoever shall exalt himself shall be abased; and he that shall humble himself{/r}{~}{r}shall be exalted.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}But woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye shut up the kingdom of{/r}{~}{r}heaven against men: for ye neither go in yourselves, neither suffer ye them that are{/r}{~}{r}entering to go in.{/r}{|}14{|}{r}Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye devour widows’ houses, and for a{/r}{~}{r}pretence make long prayer: therefore ye shall receive the greater damnation.{/r}{|}15{|}{r}Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye compass sea and land to make one{/r}{~}{r}proselyte, and when he is made, ye make him twofold more the child of hell than{/r}{~}{r}yourselves.{/r}{|}16{|}{r}Woe unto you, ye blind guides, which say, Whosoever shall swear by the temple, it is{/r}{~}{r}nothing; but whosoever shall swear by the gold of the temple, he is a debtor!{/r}{|}17{|}{r}Ye fools and blind: for whether is greater, the gold, or the temple that sanctifieth the{/r}{~}{r}gold?{/r}{|}18{|}{r}And, Whosoever shall swear by the altar, it is nothing; but whosoever sweareth by the{/r}{~}{r}gift that is upon it, he is guilty.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}Ye fools and blind: for whether is greater, the gift, or the altar that sanctifieth the{/r}{~}{r}gift?{/r}{|}20{|}{r}Whoso therefore shall swear by the altar, sweareth by it, and by all things thereon.{/r}{|}21{|}{r}And whoso shall swear by the temple, sweareth by it, and by him that dwelleth therein.{/r}{|}22{|}{r}And he that shall swear by heaven, sweareth by the throne of God, and by him that{/r}{~}{r}sitteth thereon.{/r}{|}23{|}{r}Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye pay tithe of mint and anise and{/r}{~}{r}cummin, and have omitted the weightier matters of the law, judgment, mercy, and faith:{/r}{~}{r}these ought ye to have done, and not to leave the other undone.{/r}{|}24{|}{r}Ye blind guides, which strain at a gnat, and swallow a camel.{/r}{|}25{|}{r}Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye make clean the outside of the{/r}{~}{r}cup and of the platter, but within they are full of extortion and excess.{/r}{|}26{|}{r}Thou blind Pharisee, cleanse first that which is within the cup and platter, that the{/r}{~}{r}outside of them may be clean also.{/r}{|}27{|}{r}Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye are like unto whited sepulchres,{/r}{~}{r}which indeed appear beautiful outward, but are within full of dead men’s bones, and of{/r}{~}{r}all uncleanness.{/r}{|}28{|}{r}Even so ye also outwardly appear righteous unto men, but within ye are full of hypocrisy{/r}{~}{r}and iniquity.{/r}{|}29{|}{r}Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! because ye build the tombs of the{/r}{~}{r}prophets, and garnish the sepulchres of the righteous,{/r}{|}30{|}{r}And say, If we had been in the days of our fathers, we would not have been partakers{/r}{~}{r}with them in the blood of the prophets.{/r}{|}31{|}{r}Wherefore ye be witnesses unto yourselves, that ye are the children of them which killed{/r}{~}{r}the prophets.{/r}{|}32{|}{r}Fill ye up then the measure of your fathers.{/r}{|}33{|}{r}Ye serpents, ye generation of vipers, how can ye escape the damnation of hell?{/r}{|}34{|}{r}Wherefore, behold, I send unto you prophets, and wise men, and scribes: and some of them{/r}{~}{r}ye shall kill and crucify; and some of them shall ye scourge in your synagogues, and{/r}{~}{r}persecute them from city to city:{/r}{|}35{|}{r}That upon you may come all the righteous blood shed upon the earth, from the blood of{/r}{~}{r}righteous Abel unto the blood of Zacharias son of Barachias, whom ye slew between the{/r}{~}{r}temple and the altar.{/r}{|}36{|}{r}Verily I say unto you, All these things shall come upon this generation.{/r}{|}37{|}{r}O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, thou that killest the prophets, and stonest them which are sent{/r}{~}{r}unto thee, how often would I have gathered thy children together, even as a hen{/r}{~}{r}gathereth her chickens under her wings, and ye would not!{/r}{|}38{|}{r}Behold, your house is left unto you desolate.{/r}{|}39{|}{r}For I say unto you, Ye shall not see me henceforth, till ye shall say, Blessed is he{/r}{~}{r}that cometh in the name of the Lord.{/r}";
    case 24: return s"1{|}And Jesus went out, and departed from the temple: and his disciples came to him for to{~}shew him the buildings of the temple.{|}2{|}And Jesus said unto them,{~}{r}See ye not all these things? verily I say unto you, There shall not be left here one{/r}{~}{r}stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down.{/r}{|}3{|}And as he sat upon the mount of Olives, the disciples came unto him privately, saying,{~}Tell us, when shall these things be? and what shall be the sign of thy coming, and of{~}the end of the world?{|}4{|}And Jesus answered and said unto them,{~}{r}Take heed that no man deceive you.{/r}{|}5{|}{r}For many shall come in my name, saying, I am Christ; and shall deceive many.{/r}{|}6{|}{r}And ye shall hear of wars and rumours of wars: see that ye be not troubled: for all{/r}{~}{r}these things must come to pass, but the end is not yet.{/r}{|}7{|}{r}For nation shall rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom: and there shall be{/r}{~}{r}famines, and pestilences, and earthquakes, in divers places.{/r}{|}8{|}{r}All these are the beginning of sorrows.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}Then shall they deliver you up to be afflicted, and shall kill you: and ye shall be{/r}{~}{r}hated of all nations for my name’s sake.{/r}{|}10{|}{r}And then shall many be offended, and shall betray one another, and shall hate one{/r}{~}{r}another.{/r}{|}11{|}{r}And many false prophets shall rise, and shall deceive many.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}And because iniquity shall abound, the love of many shall wax cold.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}But he that shall endure unto the end, the same shall be saved.{/r}{|}14{|}{r}And this gospel of the kingdom shall be preached in all the world for a witness unto all{/r}{~}{r}nations; and then shall the end come.{/r}{|}15{|}{r}When ye therefore shall see the abomination of desolation, spoken of by Daniel the{/r}{~}{r}prophet, stand in the holy place, (whoso readeth, let him understand:){/r}{|}16{|}{r}Then let them which be in Judaea flee into the mountains:{/r}{|}17{|}{r}Let him which is on the housetop not come down to take any thing out of his house:{/r}{|}18{|}{r}Neither let him which is in the field return back to take his clothes.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}And woe unto them that are with child, and to them that give suck in those days!{/r}{|}20{|}{r}But pray ye that your flight be not in the winter, neither on the sabbath day:{/r}{|}21{|}{r}For then shall be great tribulation, such as was not since the beginning of the world to{/r}{~}{r}this time, no, nor ever shall be.{/r}{|}22{|}{r}And except those days should be shortened, there should no flesh be saved: but for the{/r}{~}{r}elect’s sake those days shall be shortened.{/r}{|}23{|}{r}Then if any man shall say unto you, Lo, here is Christ, or there; believe it not.{/r}{|}24{|}{r}For there shall arise false Christs, and false prophets, and shall shew great signs and{/r}{~}{r}wonders; insomuch that, if it were possible, they shall deceive the very elect.{/r}{|}25{|}{r}Behold, I have told you before.{/r}{|}26{|}{r}Wherefore if they shall say unto you, Behold, he is in the desert; go not forth: behold,{/r}{~}{r}he is in the secret chambers; believe it not.{/r}{|}27{|}{r}For as the lightning cometh out of the east, and shineth even unto the west; so shall{/r}{~}{r}also the coming of the Son of man be.{/r}{|}28{|}{r}For wheresoever the carcase is, there will the eagles be gathered together.{/r}{|}29{|}{r}Immediately after the tribulation of those days shall the sun be darkened, and the moon{/r}{~}{r}shall not give her light, and the stars shall fall from heaven, and the powers of the{/r}{~}{r}heavens shall be shaken:{/r}{|}30{|}{r}And then shall appear the sign of the Son of man in heaven: and then shall all the{/r}{~}{r}tribes of the earth mourn, and they shall see the Son of man coming in the clouds of{/r}{~}{r}heaven with power and great glory.{/r}{|}31{|}{r}And he shall send his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather{/r}{~}{r}together his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other.{/r}{|}32{|}{r}Now learn a parable of the fig tree; When his branch is yet tender, and putteth forth{/r}{~}{r}leaves, ye know that summer is nigh:{/r}{|}33{|}{r}So likewise ye, when ye shall see all these things, know that it is near, even at the{/r}{~}{r}doors.{/r}{|}34{|}{r}Verily I say unto you, This generation shall not pass, till all these things be{/r}{~}{r}fulfilled.{/r}{|}35{|}{r}Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away.{/r}{|}36{|}{r}But of that day and hour knoweth no man, no, not the angels of heaven, but my Father{/r}{~}{r}only.{/r}{|}37{|}{r}But as the days of Noe were, so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.{/r}{|}38{|}{r}For as in the days that were before the flood they were eating and drinking, marrying{/r}{~}{r}and giving in marriage, until the day that Noe entered into the ark,{/r}{|}39{|}{r}And knew not until the flood came, and took them all away; so shall also the coming of{/r}{~}{r}the Son of man be.{/r}{|}40{|}{r}Then shall two be in the field; the one shall be taken, and the other left.{/r}{|}41{|}{r}Two women shall be grinding at the mill; the one shall be taken, and the other left.{/r}{|}42{|}{r}Watch therefore: for ye know not what hour your Lord doth come.{/r}{|}43{|}{r}But know this, that if the goodman of the house had known in what watch the thief would{/r}{~}{r}come, he would have watched, and would not have suffered his house to be broken up.{/r}{|}44{|}{r}Therefore be ye also ready: for in such an hour as ye think not the Son of man cometh.{/r}{|}45{|}{r}Who then is a faithful and wise servant, whom his lord hath made ruler over his{/r}{~}{r}household, to give them meat in due season?{/r}{|}46{|}{r}Blessed is that servant, whom his lord when he cometh shall find so doing.{/r}{|}47{|}{r}Verily I say unto you, That he shall make him ruler over all his goods.{/r}{|}48{|}{r}But and if that evil servant shall say in his heart, My lord delayeth his coming;{/r}{|}49{|}{r}And shall begin to smite his fellowservants, and to eat and drink with the drunken;{/r}{|}50{|}{r}The lord of that servant shall come in a day when he looketh not for him, and in an hour{/r}{~}{r}that he is not aware of,{/r}{|}51{|}{r}And shall cut him asunder, and appoint him his portion with the hypocrites: there shall{/r}{~}{r}be weeping and gnashing of teeth.{/r}";
    case 25: return s"1{|}{r}Then shall the kingdom of heaven be likened unto ten virgins, which took their lamps,{/r}{~}{r}and went forth to meet the bridegroom.{/r}{|}2{|}{r}And five of them were wise, and five were foolish.{/r}{|}3{|}{r}They that were foolish took their lamps, and took no oil with them:{/r}{|}4{|}{r}But the wise took oil in their vessels with their lamps.{/r}{|}5{|}{r}While the bridegroom tarried, they all slumbered and slept.{/r}{|}6{|}{r}And at midnight there was a cry made, Behold, the bridegroom cometh; go ye out to meet{/r}{~}{r}him.{/r}{|}7{|}{r}Then all those virgins arose, and trimmed their lamps.{/r}{|}8{|}{r}And the foolish said unto the wise, Give us of your oil; for our lamps are gone out.{/r}{|}9{|}{r}But the wise answered, saying, Not so; lest there be not enough for us and you: but go{/r}{~}{r}ye rather to them that sell, and buy for yourselves.{/r}{|}10{|}{r}And while they went to buy, the bridegroom came; and they that were ready went in with{/r}{~}{r}him to the marriage: and the door was shut.{/r}{|}11{|}{r}Afterward came also the other virgins, saying, Lord, Lord, open to us.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}But he answered and said, Verily I say unto you, I know you not.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}Watch therefore, for ye know neither the day nor the hour wherein the Son of man cometh.{/r}{|}14{|}{r}For the kingdom of heaven is as a man travelling into a far country, who called his own{/r}{~}{r}servants, and delivered unto them his goods.{/r}{|}15{|}{r}And unto one he gave five talents, to another two, and to another one; to every man{/r}{~}{r}according to his several ability; and straightway took his journey.{/r}{|}16{|}{r}Then he that had received the five talents went and traded with the same, and made them{/r}{~}{r}other five talents.{/r}{|}17{|}{r}And likewise he that had received two, he also gained other two.{/r}{|}18{|}{r}But he that had received one went and digged in the earth, and hid his lord’s money.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}After a long time the lord of those servants cometh, and reckoneth with them.{/r}{|}20{|}{r}And so he that had received five talents came and brought other five talents, saying,{/r}{~}{r}Lord, thou deliveredst unto me five talents: behold, I have gained beside them five{/r}{~}{r}talents more.{/r}{|}21{|}{r}His lord said unto him, Well done, thou good and faithful servant: thou hast been{/r}{~}{r}faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the{/r}{~}{r}joy of thy lord.{/r}{|}22{|}{r}He also that had received two talents came and said, Lord, thou deliveredst unto me two{/r}{~}{r}talents: behold, I have gained two other talents beside them.{/r}{|}23{|}{r}His lord said unto him, Well done, good and faithful servant; thou hast been faithful{/r}{~}{r}over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of{/r}{~}{r}thy lord.{/r}{|}24{|}{r}Then he which had received the one talent came and said, Lord, I knew thee that thou art{/r}{~}{r}an hard man, reaping where thou hast not sown, and gathering where thou hast not{/r}{~}{r}strawed:{/r}{|}25{|}{r}And I was afraid, and went and hid thy talent in the earth: lo, there thou hast that is{/r}{~}{r}thine.{/r}{|}26{|}{r}His lord answered and said unto him, Thou wicked and slothful servant, thou knewest that{/r}{~}{r}I reap where I sowed not, and gather where I have not strawed:{/r}{|}27{|}{r}Thou oughtest therefore to have put my money to the exchangers, and then at my coming I{/r}{~}{r}should have received mine own with usury.{/r}{|}28{|}{r}Take therefore the talent from him, and give it unto him which hath ten talents.{/r}{|}29{|}{r}For unto every one that hath shall be given, and he shall have abundance: but from him{/r}{~}{r}that hath not shall be taken away even that which he hath.{/r}{|}30{|}{r}And cast ye the unprofitable servant into outer darkness: there shall be weeping and{/r}{~}{r}gnashing of teeth.{/r}{|}31{|}{r}When the Son of man shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then{/r}{~}{r}shall he sit upon the throne of his glory:{/r}{|}32{|}{r}And before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from{/r}{~}{r}another, as a shepherd divideth his sheep from the goats:{/r}{|}33{|}{r}And he shall set the sheep on his right hand, but the goats on the left.{/r}{|}34{|}{r}Then shall the King say unto them on his right hand, Come, ye blessed of my Father,{/r}{~}{r}inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world:{/r}{|}35{|}{r}For I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me drink: I was a{/r}{~}{r}stranger, and ye took me in:{/r}{|}36{|}{r}Naked, and ye clothed me: I was sick, and ye visited me: I was in prison, and ye came{/r}{~}{r}unto me.{/r}{|}37{|}{r}Then shall the righteous answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, and fed{/r}{~}{r}thee? or thirsty, and gave thee drink?{/r}{|}38{|}{r}When saw we thee a stranger, and took thee in? or naked, and clothed thee?{/r}{|}39{|}{r}Or when saw we thee sick, or in prison, and came unto thee?{/r}{|}40{|}{r}And the King shall answer and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye have{/r}{~}{r}done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me.{/r}{|}41{|}{r}Then shall he say also unto them on the left hand, Depart from me, ye cursed, into{/r}{~}{r}everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels:{/r}{|}42{|}{r}For I was an hungred, and ye gave me no meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me no drink:{/r}{|}43{|}{r}I was a stranger, and ye took me not in: naked, and ye clothed me not: sick, and in{/r}{~}{r}prison, and ye visited me not.{/r}{|}44{|}{r}Then shall they also answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, or athirst,{/r}{~}{r}or a stranger, or naked, or sick, or in prison, and did not minister unto thee?{/r}{|}45{|}{r}Then shall he answer them, saying, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye did it not to{/r}{~}{r}one of the least of these, ye did it not to me.{/r}{|}46{|}{r}And these shall go away into everlasting punishment: but the righteous into life{/r}{~}{r}eternal.{/r}";
    case 26: return s"1{|}And it came to pass, when Jesus had finished all these sayings, he said unto his{~}disciples,{|}2{|}{r}Ye know that after two days is the feast of the passover, and the Son of man is betrayed{/r}{~}{r}to be crucified.{/r}{|}3{|}Then assembled together the chief priests, and the scribes, and the elders of the{~}people, unto the palace of the high priest, who was called Caiaphas,{|}4{|}And consulted that they might take Jesus by subtilty, and kill him.{|}5{|}But they said, Not on the feast day, lest there be an uproar among the people.{|}6{|}Now when Jesus was in Bethany, in the house of Simon the leper,{|}7{|}There came unto him a woman having an alabaster box of very precious ointment, and{~}poured it on his head, as he sat at meat.{|}8{|}But when his disciples saw it, they had indignation, saying, To what purpose is this{~}waste?{|}9{|}For this ointment might have been sold for much, and given to the poor.{|}10{|}When Jesus understood it, he said unto them,{~}{r}Why trouble ye the woman? for she hath wrought a good work upon me.{/r}{|}11{|}{r}For ye have the poor always with you; but me ye have not always.{/r}{|}12{|}{r}For in that she hath poured this ointment on my body, she did it for my burial.{/r}{|}13{|}{r}Verily I say unto you, Wheresoever this gospel shall be preached in the whole world,{/r}{~}{r}there shall also this, that this woman hath done, be told for a memorial of her.{/r}{|}14{|}Then one of the twelve, called Judas Iscariot, went unto the chief priests,{|}15{|}And said unto them, What will ye give me, and I will deliver him unto you? And they{~}covenanted with him for thirty pieces of silver.{|}16{|}And from that time he sought opportunity to betray him.{|}17{|}Now the first day of the feast of unleavened bread the disciples came to Jesus, saying{~}unto him, Where wilt thou that we prepare for thee to eat the passover?{|}18{|}And he said,{~}{r}Go into the city to such a man, and say unto him, The Master saith, My time is at hand;{/r}{~}{r}I will keep the passover at thy house with my disciples.{/r}{|}19{|}And the disciples did as Jesus had appointed them; and they made ready the passover.{|}20{|}Now when the even was come, he sat down with the twelve.{|}21{|}And as they did eat, he said,{~}{r}Verily I say unto you, that one of you shall betray me.{/r}{|}22{|}And they were exceeding sorrowful, and began every one of them to say unto him, Lord, is{~}it I?{|}23{|}And he answered and said,{~}{r}He that dippeth his hand with me in the dish, the same shall betray me.{/r}{|}24{|}{r}The Son of man goeth as it is written of him: but woe unto that man by whom the Son of{/r}{~}{r}man is betrayed! it had been good for that man if he had not been born.{/r}{|}25{|}Then Judas, which betrayed him, answered and said, Master, is it I? He said unto him,{~}{r}Thou hast said.{/r}{|}26{|}And as they were eating, Jesus took bread, and blessed it, and brake it, and gave it to{~}the disciples, and said,{~}{r}Take, eat; this is my body.{/r}{|}27{|}And he took the cup, and gave thanks, and gave it to them, saying,{~}{r}Drink ye all of it;{/r}{|}28{|}{r}For this is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many for the remission of{/r}{~}{r}sins.{/r}{|}29{|}{r}But I say unto you, I will not drink henceforth of this fruit of the vine, until that{/r}{~}{r}day when I drink it new with you in my Father’s kingdom.{/r}{|}30{|}And when they had sung an hymn, they went out into the mount of Olives.{|}31{|}Then saith Jesus unto them,{~}{r}All ye shall be offended because of me this night: for it is written, I will smite the{/r}{~}{r}shepherd, and the sheep of the flock shall be scattered abroad.{/r}{|}32{|}{r}But after I am risen again, I will go before you into Galilee.{/r}{|}33{|}Peter answered and said unto him, Though all men shall be offended because of thee, yet{~}will I never be offended.{|}34{|}Jesus said unto him,{~}{r}Verily I say unto thee, That this night, before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me{/r}{~}{r}thrice.{/r}{|}35{|}Peter said unto him, Though I should die with thee, yet will I not deny thee. Likewise{~}also said all the disciples.{|}36{|}Then cometh Jesus with them unto a place called Gethsemane, and saith unto the{~}disciples,{~}{r}Sit ye here, while I go and pray yonder.{/r}{|}37{|}And he took with him Peter and the two sons of Zebedee, and began to be sorrowful and{~}very heavy.{|}38{|}Then saith he unto them,{~}{r}My soul is exceeding sorrowful, even unto death: tarry ye here, and watch with me.{/r}{|}39{|}And he went a little further, and fell on his face, and prayed, saying,{~}{r}O my Father, if it be possible, let this cup pass from me: nevertheless not as I will,{/r}{~}{r}but as thou wilt.{/r}{|}40{|}And he cometh unto the disciples, and findeth them asleep, and saith unto Peter,{~}{r}What, could ye not watch with me one hour?{/r}{|}41{|}{r}Watch and pray, that ye enter not into temptation: the spirit indeed is willing, but the{/r}{~}{r}flesh is weak.{/r}{|}42{|}He went away again the second time, and prayed, saying,{~}{r}O my Father, if this cup may not pass away from me, except I drink it, thy will be done.{/r}{|}43{|}And he came and found them asleep again: for their eyes were heavy.{|}44{|}And he left them, and went away again, and prayed the third time, saying the same words.{|}45{|}Then cometh he to his disciples, and saith unto them,{~}{r}Sleep on now, and take your rest: behold, the hour is at hand, and the Son of man is{/r}{~}{r}betrayed into the hands of sinners.{/r}{|}46{|}{r}Rise, let us be going: behold, he is at hand that doth betray me.{/r}{|}47{|}And while he yet spake, lo, Judas, one of the twelve, came, and with him a great{~}multitude with swords and staves, from the chief priests and elders of the people.{|}48{|}Now he that betrayed him gave them a sign, saying, Whomsoever I shall kiss, that same is{~}he: hold him fast.{|}49{|}And forthwith he came to Jesus, and said, Hail, master; and kissed him.{|}50{|}And Jesus said unto him,{~}{r}Friend, wherefore art thou come?{/r}{~}Then came they, and laid hands on Jesus, and took him.{|}51{|}And, behold, one of them which were with Jesus stretched out his hand, and drew his{~}sword, and struck a servant of the high priest’s, and smote off his ear.{|}52{|}Then said Jesus unto him,{~}{r}Put up again thy sword into his place: for all they that take the sword shall perish{/r}{~}{r}with the sword.{/r}{|}53{|}{r}Thinkest thou that I cannot now pray to my Father, and he shall presently give me more{/r}{~}{r}than twelve legions of angels?{/r}{|}54{|}{r}But how then shall the scriptures be fulfilled, that thus it must be?{/r}{|}55{|}In that same hour said Jesus to the multitudes,{~}{r}Are ye come out as against a thief with swords and staves for to take me? I sat daily{/r}{~}{r}with you teaching in the temple, and ye laid no hold on me.{/r}{|}56{|}{r}But all this was done, that the scriptures of the prophets might be fulfilled.{/r}{~}Then all the disciples forsook him, and fled.{|}57{|}And they that had laid hold on Jesus led him away to Caiaphas the high priest, where the{~}scribes and the elders were assembled.{|}58{|}But Peter followed him afar off unto the high priest’s palace, and went in, and sat with{~}the servants, to see the end.{|}59{|}Now the chief priests, and elders, and all the council, sought false witness against{~}Jesus, to put him to death;{|}60{|}But found none: yea, though many false witnesses came, yet found they none. At the last{~}came two false witnesses,{|}61{|}And said, This fellow said, I am able to destroy the temple of God, and to build it in{~}three days.{|}62{|}And the high priest arose, and said unto him, Answerest thou nothing? what is it which{~}these witness against thee?{|}63{|}But Jesus held his peace. And the high priest answered and said unto him, I adjure thee{~}by the living God, that thou tell us whether thou be the Christ, the Son of God.{|}64{|}Jesus saith unto him,{~}{r}Thou hast said: nevertheless I say unto you, Hereafter shall ye see the Son of man{/r}{~}{r}sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven.{/r}{|}65{|}Then the high priest rent his clothes, saying, He hath spoken blasphemy; what further{~}need have we of witnesses? behold, now ye have heard his blasphemy.{|}66{|}What think ye? They answered and said, He is guilty of death.{|}67{|}Then did they spit in his face, and buffeted him; and others smote him with the palms of{~}their hands,{|}68{|}Saying, Prophesy unto us, thou Christ, Who is he that smote thee?{|}69{|}Now Peter sat without in the palace: and a damsel came unto him, saying, Thou also wast{~}with Jesus of Galilee.{|}70{|}But he denied before them all, saying, I know not what thou sayest.{|}71{|}And when he was gone out into the porch, another maid saw him, and said unto them that{~}were there, This fellow was also with Jesus of Nazareth.{|}72{|}And again he denied with an oath, I do not know the man.{|}73{|}And after a while came unto him they that stood by, and said to Peter, Surely thou also{~}art one of them; for thy speech bewrayeth thee.{|}74{|}Then began he to curse and to swear, saying, I know not the man. And immediately the{~}cock crew.{|}75{|}And Peter remembered the word of Jesus, which said unto him, Before the cock crow, thou{~}shalt deny me thrice. And he went out, and wept bitterly.";
    case 27: return s"1{|}When the morning was come, all the chief priests and elders of the people took counsel{~}against Jesus to put him to death:{|}2{|}And when they had bound him, they led him away, and delivered him to Pontius Pilate the{~}governor.{|}3{|}Then Judas, which had betrayed him, when he saw that he was condemned, repented himself,{~}and brought again the thirty pieces of silver to the chief priests and elders,{|}4{|}Saying, I have sinned in that I have betrayed the innocent blood. And they said, What is{~}that to us? see thou to that.{|}5{|}And he cast down the pieces of silver in the temple, and departed, and went and hanged{~}himself.{|}6{|}And the chief priests took the silver pieces, and said, It is not lawful for to put them{~}into the treasury, because it is the price of blood.{|}7{|}And they took counsel, and bought with them the potter’s field, to bury strangers in.{|}8{|}Wherefore that field was called, The field of blood, unto this day.{|}9{|}Then was fulfilled that which was spoken by Jeremy the prophet, saying, And they took{~}the thirty pieces of silver, the price of him that was valued, whom they of the children{~}of Israel did value;{|}10{|}And gave them for the potter’s field, as the Lord appointed me.{|}11{|}And Jesus stood before the governor: and the governor asked him, saying, Art thou the{~}King of the Jews? And Jesus said unto him,{~}{r}Thou sayest.{/r}{|}12{|}And when he was accused of the chief priests and elders, he answered nothing.{|}13{|}Then said Pilate unto him, Hearest thou not how many things they witness against thee?{|}14{|}And he answered him to never a word; insomuch that the governor marvelled greatly.{|}15{|}Now at that feast the governor was wont to release unto the people a prisoner, whom they{~}would.{|}16{|}And they had then a notable prisoner, called Barabbas.{|}17{|}Therefore when they were gathered together, Pilate said unto them, Whom will ye that I{~}release unto you? Barabbas, or Jesus which is called Christ?{|}18{|}For he knew that for envy they had delivered him.{|}19{|}When he was set down on the judgment seat, his wife sent unto him, saying, Have thou{~}nothing to do with that just man: for I have suffered many things this day in a dream{~}because of him.{|}20{|}But the chief priests and elders persuaded the multitude that they should ask Barabbas,{~}and destroy Jesus.{|}21{|}The governor answered and said unto them, Whether of the twain will ye that I release{~}unto you? They said, Barabbas.{|}22{|}Pilate saith unto them, What shall I do then with Jesus which is called Christ? They all{~}say unto him, Let him be crucified.{|}23{|}And the governor said, Why, what evil hath he done? But they cried out the more, saying,{~}Let him be crucified.{|}24{|}When Pilate saw that he could prevail nothing, but that rather a tumult was made, he{~}took water, and washed his hands before the multitude, saying, I am innocent of the{~}blood of this just person: see ye to it.{|}25{|}Then answered all the people, and said, His blood be on us, and on our children.{|}26{|}Then released he Barabbas unto them: and when he had scourged Jesus, he delivered him to{~}be crucified.{|}27{|}Then the soldiers of the governor took Jesus into the common hall, and gathered unto him{~}the whole band of soldiers.{|}28{|}And they stripped him, and put on him a scarlet robe.{|}29{|}And when they had platted a crown of thorns, they put it upon his head, and a reed in{~}his right hand: and they bowed the knee before him, and mocked him, saying, Hail, King{~}of the Jews!{|}30{|}And they spit upon him, and took the reed, and smote him on the head.{|}31{|}And after that they had mocked him, they took the robe off from him, and put his own{~}raiment on him, and led him away to crucify him.{|}32{|}And as they came out, they found a man of Cyrene, Simon by name: him they compelled to{~}bear his cross.{|}33{|}And when they were come unto a place called Golgotha, that is to say, a place of a{~}skull,{|}34{|}They gave him vinegar to drink mingled with gall: and when he had tasted thereof, he{~}would not drink.{|}35{|}And they crucified him, and parted his garments, casting lots: that it might be{~}fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, They parted my garments among them, and upon{~}my vesture did they cast lots.{|}36{|}And sitting down they watched him there;{|}37{|}And set up over his head his accusation written, THIS IS JESUS THE KING OF THE JEWS.{|}38{|}Then were there two thieves crucified with him, one on the right hand, and another on{~}the left.{|}39{|}And they that passed by reviled him, wagging their heads,{|}40{|}And saying, Thou that destroyest the temple, and buildest it in three days, save{~}thyself. If thou be the Son of God, come down from the cross.{|}41{|}Likewise also the chief priests mocking him, with the scribes and elders, said,{|}42{|}He saved others; himself he cannot save. If he be the King of Israel, let him now come{~}down from the cross, and we will believe him.{|}43{|}He trusted in God; let him deliver him now, if he will have him: for he said, I am the{~}Son of God.{|}44{|}The thieves also, which were crucified with him, cast the same in his teeth.{|}45{|}Now from the sixth hour there was darkness over all the land unto the ninth hour.{|}46{|}And about the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying,{~}{r}Eli, Eli, lama sabachthani?{/r}{~}that is to say, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?{|}47{|}Some of them that stood there, when they heard that, said, This man calleth for Elias.{|}48{|}And straightway one of them ran, and took a spunge, and filled it with vinegar, and put{~}it on a reed, and gave him to drink.{|}49{|}The rest said, Let be, let us see whether Elias will come to save him.{|}50{|}Jesus, when he had cried again with a loud voice, yielded up the ghost.{|}51{|}And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom; and{~}the earth did quake, and the rocks rent;{|}52{|}And the graves were opened; and many bodies of the saints which slept arose,{|}53{|}And came out of the graves after his resurrection, and went into the holy city, and{~}appeared unto many.{|}54{|}Now when the centurion, and they that were with him, watching Jesus, saw the earthquake,{~}and those things that were done, they feared greatly, saying, Truly this was the Son of{~}God.{|}55{|}And many women were there beholding afar off, which followed Jesus from Galilee,{~}ministering unto him:{|}56{|}Among which was Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James and Joses, and the mother{~}of Zebedee’s children.{|}57{|}When the even was come, there came a rich man of Arimathæa, named Joseph, who also{~}himself was Jesus’ disciple:{|}58{|}He went to Pilate, and begged the body of Jesus. Then Pilate commanded the body to be{~}delivered.{|}59{|}And when Joseph had taken the body, he wrapped it in a clean linen cloth,{|}60{|}And laid it in his own new tomb, which he had hewn out in the rock: and he rolled a{~}great stone to the door of the sepulchre, and departed.{|}61{|}And there was Mary Magdalene, and the other Mary, sitting over against the sepulchre.{|}62{|}Now the next day, that followed the day of the preparation, the chief priests and{~}Pharisees came together unto Pilate,{|}63{|}Saying, Sir, we remember that that deceiver said, while he was yet alive, After three{~}days I will rise again.{|}64{|}Command therefore that the sepulchre be made sure until the third day, lest his{~}disciples come by night, and steal him away, and say unto the people, He is risen from{~}the dead: so the last error shall be worse than the first.{|}65{|}Pilate said unto them, Ye have a watch: go your way, make it as sure as ye can.{|}66{|}So they went, and made the sepulchre sure, sealing the stone, and setting a watch.";
    case 28: return s"1{|}In the end of the sabbath, as it began to dawn toward the first day of the week, came{~}Mary Magdalene and the other Mary to see the sepulchre.{|}2{|}And, behold, there was a great earthquake: for the angel of the Lord descended from{~}heaven, and came and rolled back the stone from the door, and sat upon it.{|}3{|}His countenance was like lightning, and his raiment white as snow:{|}4{|}And for fear of him the keepers did shake, and became as dead men.{|}5{|}And the angel answered and said unto the women, Fear not ye: for I know that ye seek{~}Jesus, which was crucified.{|}6{|}He is not here: for he is risen, as he said. Come, see the place where the Lord lay.{|}7{|}And go quickly, and tell his disciples that he is risen from the dead; and, behold, he{~}goeth before you into Galilee; there shall ye see him: lo, I have told you.{|}8{|}And they departed quickly from the sepulchre with fear and great joy; and did run to{~}bring his disciples word.{|}9{|}And as they went to tell his disciples, behold, Jesus met them, saying,{~}{r}All hail.{/r}{~}And they came and held him by the feet, and worshipped him.{|}10{|}Then said Jesus unto them,{~}{r}Be not afraid: go tell my brethren that they go into Galilee, and there shall they see{/r}{~}{r}me.{/r}{|}11{|}Now when they were going, behold, some of the watch came into the city, and shewed unto{~}the chief priests all the things that were done.{|}12{|}And when they were assembled with the elders, and had taken counsel, they gave large{~}money unto the soldiers,{|}13{|}Saying, Say ye, His disciples came by night, and stole him away while we slept.{|}14{|}And if this come to the governor’s ears, we will persuade him, and secure you.{|}15{|}So they took the money, and did as they were taught: and this saying is commonly{~}reported among the Jews until this day.{|}16{|}Then the eleven disciples went away into Galilee, into a mountain where Jesus had{~}appointed them.{|}17{|}And when they saw him, they worshipped him: but some doubted.{|}18{|}And Jesus came and spake unto them, saying,{~}{r}All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth.{/r}{|}19{|}{r}Go ye therefore, and teach all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father, and of{/r}{~}{r}the Son, and of the Holy Ghost:{/r}{|}20{|}{r}Teaching them to observe all things whatsoever I have commanded you: and, lo, I am with{/r}{~}{r}you alway, even unto the end of the world.{/r}{~}Amen.";
    default: return s"";
  };
}
